Re 纠正叙事失效 — 既无法说 BM25 害人，也无法说 embedding 救人。整个 mining strategy 维度在此 scale 下坍缩为 noise。\n\n  CodeQL pipeline 保留为 practical contribution + representation geometry analysis 保留为 explanatory tool（解释 WHY strategies fail to differentiate）。UniXcoder null 成为 corroborating evidence。SWE-bench 不提（OOD failure，R@1=0.04）。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_001: M1 CodeQL Extraction (DONE)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"M1 全量 CodeQL 提取\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_001\"\n    description: \"5K SWE-smith repos data-flow extraction + connected vs gold statistics\"\n    expected_results:\n      status: DONE\n      structural_data_rate: 0.36\n      repos_with_output: 123\n      zero_timeout_rate: true\n      z_pct_mean: 0.78\n    result_rationale: |\n      基础设施实验，结果与 tier 无关。CodeQL pipeline 在 worst tier 下保留为 practical contribution：\n      0% timeout、78% connected-not-gold rate、123/131 repo coverage 证明 scope-bounded \n      inter-procedural data-flow analysis 在工业级 codebase 上可行。这是 reframe 后论文的\n      supporting methodology 贡献，不受 mining strategy null result 影响。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"不受 tier 影响。作为 reframe 后论文的 Section 3 (Methodology) 支撑。\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_002: M2 Full Qwen Training (remaining runs)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"M2 全量 Qwen 4-strategy × 3-seed 训练\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_002\"\n    description: \"Qwen2.5-Coder-3B LoRA: random/embed/dataflow/bm25 × seeds 42/43/44。6 runs 已完成（random ×3, embed s43/s44, dataflow s43），预测剩余 6 runs。\"\n    expected_results:\n      # === 已完成 runs（actual data）===\n      random_s42_R1: 0.5527\n      random_s43_R1: 0.5554\n      random_s44_R1: 0.6009\n      random_mean: 0.5697\n      random_std_pp: 2.71\n      embedding_distance_s43_R1: 0.5606\n      embedding_distance_s44_R1: 0.5942\n      dataflow_aware_s43_R1: 0.5564\n      # === 预测 runs ===\n      embedding_distance_s42_R1: 0.549\n      dataflow_aware_s42_R1: 0.548\n      dataflow_aware_s44_R1: 0.575\n      bm25_s42_R1: 0.555\n      bm25_s43_R1: 0.558\n      bm25_s44_R1: 0.597\n      # === 汇总统计 ===\n      embed_mean: 0.568\n      embed_std_pp: 2.3\n      embed_vs_random_mean_delta_pp: -0.17\n      dataflow_mean: 0.560\n      dataflow_std_pp: 1.4\n      dataflow_vs_random_mean_delta_pp: -0.99\n      bm25_mean: 0.570\n      bm25_std_pp: 2.3\n      bm25_vs_random_mean_delta_pp: +0.03\n      # === 统计检验 ===\n      embed_vs_random_paired_deltas: [-0.37, +0.52, -0.67]\n      embed_vs_random_bootstrap_95ci: [-0.92, +0.58]\n      embed_vs_random_ci_includes_zero: true\n      dataflow_vs_random_paired_deltas: [-0.47, +0.10, -2.59]\n      dataflow_vs_random_bootstrap_95ci: [-2.36, +0.58]\n      dataflow_vs_random_ci_includes_zero: true\n      bm25_vs_random_paired_deltas: [+0.23, +0.26, -0.39]\n      bm25_vs_random_bootstrap_95ci: [-0.55, +0.59]\n      bm25_vs_random_ci_includes_zero: true\n      cross_seed_std_dominates_strategy: true\n      seed_noise_to_strategy_ratio: 4.6\n    result_rationale: |\n      Worst tier 核心预测：all 3 mining strategies 与 random 不可区分。\n\n      embed_s42 预测 0.549（略低于 random 0.5527）：s42 使用 3-epoch regime（无 early stopping），\n      更长训练使 embed 的 hard negatives 导致轻微 overfitting。Qwen pos_sim=0.9855（saturated），\n      embedding-distance negatives 选自同一 cosine cone 内的样本，与 random 自然产生的 hard \n      negatives 信息量相当。s42 已有的 embed pilot（0.5557）在 pool=8 val set 上显示 +2pp，\n      但 full-scale training data 使 random baseline 足够强，消除了 marginal advantage。\n\n      dataflow_s42 预测 0.548：structural filtering 在 full-scale data 中被稀释。34% \n      structural data rate 意味着 66% 的 query 回退到 BM25-based selection，structural \n      signal 被 fallback noise 淹没。full-scale random 已包含足够 naturally hard negatives，\n      dataflow filtering 无法提供额外区分度。\n\n      dataflow_s44 预测 0.575（vs random 0.6009 = -2.59pp）：s44 的 val split 系统性偏易\n      （所有策略 R@1 更高），但 random s44 异常获益更多——可能因为 easy split 中 random \n      negatives 恰好足够 hard（pool 刚好困难度适中），而 dataflow 的 structural filtering \n      反而排除了一些有用的 borderline negatives。\n\n      bm25 ≈ random（+0.03pp mean）：BM25 overlap 分析已显示 bm25 与 embedding negatives \n      87.1% 重叠（k=50 level）。在 full-scale training 中，BM25-selected negatives 与 \n      random sampling 的差异被大量训练数据的多样性所稀释。BM25 既不 harm（反驳 MVP \n      artifact）也不 help（mining strategy 维度在此 scale 下无效）。\n\n      关键统计论证：cross-seed std（2.71pp for random）是 within-seed strategy delta \n      mean_abs（0.59pp for embed）的 4.6 倍。3 seeds 的 bootstrap 95% CI 全部包含零。\n      结论：在 n=3 seeds 下，无法拒绝 \"mining strategy effect = 0\" 的零假设。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Qwen2.5-Coder-3B R@1 (best_by_R@1, pool=8)\"\n        columns: [Strategy, s42, s43, s44, \"Mean±Std\", \"Δ vs Random\"]\n        rows:\n          - [random, 0.5527, 0.5554, 0.6009, \"0.5697±0.027\", \"—\"]\n          - [embedding_distance, \"0.549*\", 0.5606, 0.5942, \"0.568±0.023\", \"-0.17pp\"]\n          - [dataflow_aware, \"0.548*\", 0.5564, \"0.575*\", \"0.560±0.014\", \"-0.99pp\"]\n          - [bm25, \"0.555*\", \"0.558*\", \"0.597*\", \"0.570±0.023\", \"+0.03pp\"]\n        note: \"* = predicted. All strategy vs random 95% CIs include zero.\"\n      - name: \"Table 2: Paired within-seed strategy deltas (pp)\"\n        columns: [Comparison, s42, s43, s44, Mean, \"95% CI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"embed−random\", \"-0.37\", \"+0.52\", \"-0.67\", \"-0.17\", \"[-0.92, +0.58]\"]\n          - [\"dataflow−random\", \"-0.47\", \"+0.10\", \"-2.59\", \"-0.99\", \"[-2.36, +0.58]\"]\n          - [\"bm25−random\", \"+0.23\", \"+0.26\", \"-0.39\", \"+0.03\", \"[-0.55, +0.59]\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 1a: Paired delta plot — within-seed embed−random 和 dataflow−random deltas with 95% bootstrap CIs，显示所有 CI 跨越零线\"\n      - \"Fig 1b: Seed vs Strategy variance decomposition bar chart — cross-seed std (2.71pp) vs mean strategy delta (<0.5pp)，显示 seed 主导\"\n    analysis: |\n      Qwen 全量训练结果确认 mining strategy effect 在此 scale 下为 noise。\n      3 个核心发现：\n      1. Embed vs random sign-inconsistent across seeds（s43 正, s42/s44 负）→ 不可靠\n      2. Dataflow 因 fallback dilution（66% 无 structural data）+ natural random hardness \n         而系统性略低于 random\n      3. BM25 ≈ random，排除了 CoCoHaNeRe narrative（BM25 既不害人也不帮人）\n\n      Cross-seed std 4.6x > strategy effect：paired within-seed comparison 是唯一\n      合理的分析方法，但即使 paired 后，CI 仍包含零。\n\n      Checkpoint criterion divergence 贡献更大发现：s43 的 val_loss-best（step 500, \n      R@1=0.5357）和 R@1-best（step 1500, R@1=0.5554）差 1.97pp，是 strategy effect 的 \n      3.3 倍。此 methodological finding 成为 worst tier 论文的核心贡献。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_003: SWE-bench Lite Evaluation (DONE, failed)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"SWE-bench Lite end-to-end 评估\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003\"\n    description: \"3 strategies × best checkpoint on SWE-bench Lite 300 instances\"\n    expected_results:\n      status: DONE_FAILED\n      random_s42_R1: 0.04\n      random_s42_R5: 0.11\n      random_s42_R10: 0.14\n      bm25_baseline_R1: 0.2733\n      delta_vs_bm25: -23.33\n      note: \"Neural retriever OOD 泛化完全失败，已放弃\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      SWE-bench 使用 12 个 popular Python repos，与 SWE-smith 5K repos 的分布完全不同。\n      Contrastive model 在 SWE-smith 内部验证集上 R@1=0.55，但 OOD 场景下坍缩至 0.04，\n      远低于 BM25 baseline（0.2733）。\n\n      Worst tier 下此结果强化了 negative narrative：\n      1. 即使 mining strategy 在 in-distribution 上有微小差异，OOD 场景下完全不保留\n      2. 无法做 downstream task evaluation，缺少 extrinsic validation\n      3. Reviewer 会指出：如果 retriever 连 BM25 都不如，mining strategy 的讨论毫无意义\n      \n      Director decision：放弃 SWE-bench，不再重跑。外部验证改用 RepoBench-R（plan_004）。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"SWE-bench 在 worst tier 论文中不提。OOD failure 是已知局限但不影响 in-distribution methodology contribution。\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_004: RepoBench-R Cross-file Retrieval\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"RepoBench-R cross-file retrieval 评估\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: \"Retrieval-only evaluation on RepoBench-R test_easy (pool~6) 和 test_hard (pool~18)，3 strategies × 3 seeds × 2 encoders with 95% CIs\"\n    expected_results:\n      # === Qwen test_easy (pool~6) ===\n      qwen_easy_random_R1_mean: 0.875\n      qwen_easy_embed_R1_mean: 0.870\n      qwen_easy_dataflow_R1_mean: 0.868\n      qwen_easy_strategy_range_pp: 0.7\n      # === Qwen test_hard (pool~18) ===\n      qwen_hard_random_R1_mean: 0.510\n      qwen_hard_embed_R1_mean: 0.507\n      qwen_hard_dataflow_R1_mean: 0.503\n      qwen_hard_strategy_range_pp: 0.7\n      # === StarCoder test_easy ===\n      starcoder_easy_random_R1_mean: 0.820\n      starcoder_easy_embed_R1_mean: 0.815\n      starcoder_easy_dataflow_R1_mean: 0.810\n      starcoder_easy_strategy_range_pp: 1.0\n      # === StarCoder test_hard ===\n      starcoder_hard_random_R1_mean: 0.430\n      starcoder_hard_embed_R1_mean: 0.425\n      starcoder_hard_dataflow_R1_mean: 0.418\n      starcoder_hard_strategy_range_pp: 1.2\n      # === 统计 ===\n      pool_size_effect_easy_vs_hard_pp: 36.5\n      strategy_effect_within_pool_pp: \"<1.2\"\n      pool_dominates_strategy_ratio: \">30x\"\n      all_95ci_include_zero: true\n      repobench_embed_vs_random_mean_pp: -0.35\n    result_rationale: |\n      RepoBench-R 的 pool size effect 完全吞没 strategy effect：\n\n      test_easy（pool~6）：接近 ceiling（R@1 > 0.82），所有策略 ≈ 同等表现。Pool 太小，\n      即使是 random-trained model 也能在 6 个候选中找到正确答案。策略差异 <1pp，不可检测。\n\n      test_hard（pool~18）：R@1 降至 0.42-0.51，但策略排序仍不稳定。Pool=18 相比 \n      SWE-smith val pool=8 更大，但仍不足以放大 <0.5pp 的策略差异。\n\n      关键论据：pool size 从 6→18 造成 R@1 下降 ~36.5pp（Qwen），而策略差异 <1.2pp。\n      Pool size effect 是 strategy effect 的 30x+。这直接支持 worst tier narrative：\n      \"任何声称 mining strategy 有效的实验都必须控制 pool size，否则 reported effect \n      可能完全是 pool size artifact。\"\n\n      Cross-seed 95% CI 全部包含零，确认 SWE-smith 上的 null result 在 RepoBench-R \n      上同样成立。RepoBench-R 无法作为 positive external validation——只能作为额外的 \n      null evidence。\n\n      对 worst tier 论文的影响：RepoBench-R 从 \"corroborating second benchmark\" 变为 \n      \"additional evidence for null result\"。论文可以说 \"Our null finding generalizes \n      beyond SWE-smith to RepoBench-R cross-file retrieval.\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: RepoBench-R R@1 (Qwen, mean±std across 3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [Strategy, \"test_easy (pool~6)\", \"test_hard (pool~18)\", \"Δ (easy−hard)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [random, \"0.875±0.015\", \"0.510±0.020\", \"36.5pp\"]\n          - [embedding_distance, \"0.870±0.014\", \"0.507±0.019\", \"36.3pp\"]\n          - [dataflow_aware, \"0.868±0.016\", \"0.503±0.021\", \"36.5pp\"]\n        note: \"Pool size effect (~36pp) >> strategy effect (<1pp)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 2: Grouped bar chart — R@1 by strategy for test_easy vs test_hard，error bars showing 95% CI，视觉证明 pool size 主导\"\n    analysis: |\n      RepoBench-R 确认 null result 的 external validity。Pool size effect (36pp) 完全\n      吞没 strategy effect (<1.2pp)，比 SWE-smith pool=8 上的 null 更进一步证明：\n      当 pool size 增大时，strategy 差异不仅不放大反而被压缩。\n\n      这一发现直接支撑 plan_019 的 pool size sensitivity analysis，共同构成 worst tier \n      论文的重要论据：mining strategy effect 是 scale-dependent artifact，在 realistic \n      pool sizes 下完全消失。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_005: Stratified Analysis\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Embedding vs random 深度分层分析\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: \"按 5 个维度分层：repo size / pool size / query-pos similarity / structural data availability / neg_difficulty quartile\"\n    expected_results:\n      # === Stratum 1: repo size ===\n      small_lt50_embed_vs_random_pp: +0.3\n      medium_50_200_embed_vs_random_pp: -0.2\n      large_200_500_embed_vs_random_pp: -0.4\n      xlarge_500plus_embed_vs_random_pp: -0.1\n      repo_size_trend: \"no monotonic pattern\"\n      # === Stratum 2: structural data availability ===\n      rich_dataflow_embed_vs_random_pp: -0.5\n      no_dataflow_embed_vs_random_pp: -0.1\n      confound_note: \"rich_dataflow 99.3% in large/xlarge repos — cannot isolate\"\n      # === Stratum 3: neg_difficulty quartile ===\n      q1_easiest_embed_vs_random_pp: +0.2\n      q2_embed_vs_random_pp: -0.3\n      q3_embed_vs_random_pp: -0.1\n      q4_hardest_embed_vs_random_pp: -0.2\n      difficulty_trend: \"no monotonic relationship\"\n      # === Stratum 4: pool size ===\n      small_pool_embed_vs_random_pp: +0.4\n      large_pool_embed_vs_random_pp: -0.3\n      pool_size_confounded_with_repo: true\n      # === Stratum 5: query-positive similarity ===\n      high_sim_embed_vs_random_pp: -0.3\n      low_sim_embed_vs_random_pp: +0.1\n      # === 总体 ===\n      any_stratum_significant: false\n      all_ci_include_zero: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      Worst tier 下分层分析的核心发现：没有任何 stratum 显示 consistent strategy advantage。\n\n      repo size 分层无单调趋势：small repos 中 embed 微正（+0.3pp），是因为 pool size \n      小时 mining signal 偶然有效；但 medium 和 large repos 中 embed 微负，因为 full-scale \n      random baseline 已足够强。这些差异全部在 noise floor 内（CI 跨越零）。\n\n      structural data availability 分层被 confound 污染：99.3% 的 rich-dataflow instances \n      来自 large/xlarge repos，small repos 中完全不存在。无法隔离 dataflow richness 的\n      独立效应——observed pattern 完全可能是 repo size effect。\n\n      neg_difficulty quartile 分析无单调关系：如果 mining strategy 通过 difficulty \n      gradient 帮助学习，Q4（hardest negatives）应显示最大 improvement。但 worst tier 下 \n      Q4 反而微负（-0.2pp），Q1（easiest）微正（+0.2pp）——完全 inconsistent with \n      difficulty gradient hypothesis。\n\n      所有分层的 CI 均包含零。结论：不存在任何 subpopulation 中 mining strategy \n      consistently helps。Null result 是 uniform，不是被 averaging 掩盖的 heterogeneous \n      effect。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 4: Stratified embed−random delta (pp, Qwen mean across seeds)\"\n        columns: [Stratum, \"Δ R@1 (pp)\", \"95% CI\", N]\n        rows:\n          - [\"small (<50 files)\", \"+0.3\", \"[-1.2, +1.8]\", \"~500\"]\n          - [\"medium (50-200)\", \"-0.2\", \"[-1.4, +1.0]\", \"~4000\"]\n          - [\"large (200-500)\", \"-0.4\", \"[-1.6, +0.8]\", \"~13600\"]\n          - [\"xlarge (500+)\", \"-0.1\", \"[-0.9, +0.7]\", \"~26000\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 3: Stratified delta forest plot — embed−random delta by stratum with 95% CIs，所有 CI 跨越零线\"\n      - \"Fig 4: Heatmap of dataflow richness × repo size cross-tabulation，显示 99.3% confound\"\n    analysis: |\n      分层分析排除了 \"null result is caused by heterogeneous effects averaging out\" \n      的可能性。每个 stratum 单独看都是 null，不存在隐藏的 positive subgroup。\n\n      neg_difficulty quartile 分析进一步动摇了 hard negative mining 的理论基础：\n      if difficulty gradient doesn't monotonically predict improvement，then the entire \n      premise of \"harder negatives → better learning\" is questionable at this scale。\n\n      structural data confound（99.3% in large repos）意味着即使 dataflow strategy \n      在某个 stratum 有微弱优势，也无法归因于 structural information 本身，可能仅是 \n      repo size effect。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_007: Hop Depth Ablation\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"1-hop vs 2-hop vs 3-hop call-graph bounding 消融\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: \"比较不同 call-graph hop depth 对 dataflow-aware mining 的影响\"\n    expected_results:\n      hop1_R1_mean: 0.559\n      hop2_R1_mean: 0.560\n      hop3_R1_mean: 0.558\n      hop_range_pp: 0.2\n      all_vs_random_ci_include_zero: true\n      trend: \"no significant effect of hop depth\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Worst tier 下 hop depth 无效，因为 dataflow-aware strategy 本身就 ≈ random。\n      改变 structural filtering 的粒度（1-hop vs 3-hop）不会改变一个本质上无效策略的效果。\n\n      1-hop 和 3-hop 的区别是 connected file set 的大小：1-hop 更保守（fewer connected \n      files → more candidate negatives），3-hop 更激进（more connected files → fewer \n      candidate negatives）。但在 worst tier 下，无论怎么划分 connected vs disconnected，\n      最终选出的 negatives 与 random 相比都不提供额外 training signal。\n\n      原因：pretrained Qwen geometry 已 saturated（pos_sim=0.9855），negatives 的 structural \n      provenance 不影响 cosine similarity gradient。模型在 embedding space 中看不出 \n      structurally-connected 和 disconnected files 的区别。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S1: Bar chart — R@1 by hop depth (1/2/3) with error bars，显示 flat pattern\"\n    analysis: \"支持 worst tier narrative：structural signal 在 pretrained geometry saturated 时无法提供额外 training gradient。\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_008: Training Data Size Scaling\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"训练数据规模 scaling（1K/3K/5K/11K instances）\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: \"比较不同数据规模下 strategy ranking 是否变化\"\n    expected_results:\n      # === embed−random delta at each scale ===\n      scale_1K_embed_vs_random_pp: +1.2\n      scale_3K_embed_vs_random_pp: +0.5\n      scale_5K_embed_vs_random_pp: +0.2\n      scale_11K_embed_vs_random_pp: -0.17\n      # === trend ===\n      delta_trend: \"monotonically decreasing\"\n      delta_hits_zero_at: \"~4K instances\"\n      pilot_vs_full_degradation_explained: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      这是 worst tier 论文（方向 2: negative result study）的核心 figure。\n\n      Scaling analysis 预测：embed−random delta 随 data size 单调递减，在 ~4K instances \n      处穿越零线。这解释了 pilot（~2K instances）→ full scale（~11K）的 degradation pattern：\n\n      At 1K: random baseline 较弱（training set 小，naturally hard negatives 稀少），\n      embedding mining 通过 targeted selection 能显著补充 hard negatives。Delta ≈ +1.2pp。\n\n      At 3K: random baseline 变强，embedding mining marginal advantage 缩小到 +0.5pp。\n\n      At 5K+: random sampling 从足够大的 corpus 中已自动包含 naturally hard negatives \n      （概率论：如果 corpus 中有 p=3% 的 files 与 query cosine similarity > 0.96，\n      随机抽 7 个 negatives 的概率 1-(1-0.03)^7 ≈ 19% 至少包含一个），mining 的 \n      marginal value 趋近于零。\n\n      At 11K (full scale): random baseline 足够强，embed mining 反而可能因为过度集中在 \n      hard region 而导致轻微 overfitting。Delta ≈ -0.17pp。\n\n      这一 scaling curve 是 worst tier 论文的 Fig 5 (main figure for Direction 2)，\n      提供了 mechanistic explanation for why pilot results don't replicate。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: Strategy delta (embed−random) vs training data size\"\n        columns: [Data Size, \"Δ R@1 (pp)\", \"95% CI\", \"Random R@1 baseline\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"1K\", \"+1.2\", \"[+0.1, +2.3]\", \"0.48\"]\n          - [\"3K\", \"+0.5\", \"[-0.4, +1.4]\", \"0.52\"]\n          - [\"5K\", \"+0.2\", \"[-0.7, +1.1]\", \"0.54\"]\n          - [\"11K (full)\", \"-0.17\", \"[-0.92, +0.58]\", \"0.570\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 5 (main): Scaling curve — embed−random delta (pp) vs training data size (log scale)，with 95% CI shading，显示 delta 从 +1.2pp 单调递减至 ~0pp，穿越零线在 ~4K\"\n      - \"Fig 5 inset: Random baseline R@1 vs data size，显示 random 随 data size 单调递增\"\n    analysis: |\n      Scaling analysis 提供了 worst tier 论文的核心 explanatory framework：\n\n      \"Hard negative mining is a data-efficiency technique, not a quality-improvement \n      technique. Its benefit is inversely proportional to training data size because \n      larger corpora naturally contain hard negatives through random sampling.\"\n\n      这一 framing 将 null result 从 \"our method doesn't work\" 转化为 \"we discovered \n      a scaling law for mining effectiveness\"，具有独立的科学价值。\n\n      与 representation geometry analysis 结合：pretrained decoder-only encoders 的\n      near-isotropic representation space 使 random sampling 更有效地覆盖 hard region，\n      进一步减少 targeted mining 的 marginal value。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_009: Fusion Head Ablation\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Fusion head 消融（embedding-only / structural / combined）\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_009\"\n    description: \"测试 structural features 作为 fusion head 输入是否有独立贡献\"\n    expected_results:\n      embedding_only_R1: 0.569\n      structural_only_R1: 0.340\n      combined_R1: 0.571\n      structural_contribution_pp: +0.2\n      structural_contribution_significant: false\n    result_rationale: |\n      Worst tier 下 structural features 的独立贡献微不足道：\n\n      embedding-only 已经非常强（R@1≈0.569，接近 random baseline）。Pretrained decoder-only \n      encoder 的 embedding 质量已经捕获了大部分 file-level similarity signal。\n\n      structural-only（仅用 dataflow features）R@1≈0.340：structural graph features \n      单独提供一些 signal（比 random guessing 强），但远不如 learned embeddings。\n\n      combined（fusion head）R@1≈0.571：几乎无提升（+0.2pp），因为 embedding 已经是 \n      dominant feature，structural features 被 attention weights 自动降权。\n\n      这一结果支持 worst tier narrative：\"pretrained representation quality makes \n      auxiliary features marginal\"。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Confirms that pretrained embeddings dominate. Structural features as fusion input provide no meaningful lift.\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_010: Dataflow-distance Weighted Negatives\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Dataflow-distance weighted negatives vs binary connected/disconnected\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: \"连续权重 vs 二值分类对 dataflow mining 质量的影响\"\n    expected_results:\n      binary_R1: 0.560\n      weighted_R1: 0.558\n      delta_pp: -0.2\n      ci_includes_zero: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      Weighted vs binary 区别在于 negative selection 的粒度：binary 只区分 connected/disconnected，\n      weighted 按 dataflow distance（hop count）给 negatives 赋予连续权重。\n\n      Worst tier 下两者无差异：dataflow strategy 本身 ≈ random，refinement within a null \n      strategy 不会产生 positive effect。Whether you weight by distance or use binary \n      cutoff，最终 selected negatives 在 embedding space 中与 random 不可区分。\n\n      The fundamental issue is not selection granularity but signal relevance：at full scale，\n      structural distance doesn't predict embedding difficulty in a way that improves training。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Minor ablation confirming that refinements to the dataflow strategy don't rescue the null result.\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_011: Failure Analysis\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Failure analysis：50 SweRank/BM25 failures\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: \"分析 50 个 retrieval failure cases，分类 dataflow 是否能帮助\"\n    expected_results:\n      total_failures_analyzed: 50\n      dataflow_could_help: 8\n      dataflow_irrelevant: 32\n      dataflow_would_hurt: 10\n      net_dataflow_potential: \"negative\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Worst tier 下 failure analysis 强化 null result：\n\n      50 个 BM25 failure cases 中：\n      - 8 个（16%）dataflow 能潜在帮助：gold file 在 connected set 中，BM25 排名低\n      - 32 个（64%）dataflow 无关：gold file 要么不在 connected set 中（因为 structural \n        data rate 仅 34%），要么 BM25 已正确排高\n      - 10 个（20%）dataflow 反而有害：structural filtering 排除了 lexically similar \n        但 structurally disconnected 的 gold files\n\n      Net dataflow potential 为负：能帮助的 cases（16%）少于会伤害的 cases（20%）。\n      这与 macro-level null result 一致：dataflow mining 的 structural signal 在 \n      case-by-case 分析中也显示不出 systematic advantage。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Qualitative evidence supporting the quantitative null. Dataflow's structural filtering is as likely to exclude relevant files as to identify hard negatives.\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_012: Qualitative Examples\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"定性 examples：5-10 cases where structural negatives changed retrieval\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: \"展示 structural negatives 改变 retrieval outcome 的具体 cases\"\n    expected_results:\n      positive_examples_found: 3\n      negative_examples_found: 4\n      neutral_examples: 3\n      net_impression: \"mixed — no consistent pattern\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Worst tier 下 qualitative examples 呈现 mixed picture：\n\n      能找到 3 个 positive examples（dataflow-trained model 正确 retrieve 了 structurally \n      connected file），但同时有 4 个 negative examples（dataflow training 导致 model \n      过度偏向 structurally connected files，遗漏 lexically similar gold files）。\n\n      这些 examples 在 worst tier 论文中的定位从 \"showcase of structural benefit\" 变为 \n      \"illustrative cases showing mixed signal\"，支持 \"structural mining is not reliably \n      beneficial\" 的 narrative。\n\n      3 个 neutral examples 中策略选择对 retrieval outcome 无影响（all strategies retrieve \n      same files），进一步支持 null result。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S2: Side-by-side retrieval comparison for 2 positive and 2 negative examples，showing both benefits and harms of structural negatives\"\n    analysis: \"Cherry-picked examples can tell any story. The balanced mixed picture supports the null result narrative.\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_013: StarCoder Full-scale Training (remaining runs)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"M2 全量 StarCoder 3-strategy × 3-seed 训练\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: \"StarCoder2-3B LoRA: random/embed/dataflow × seeds 42/43/44。4 runs 已完成（random ×3, embed s42），预测剩余 5 runs。\"\n    expected_results:\n      # === 已完成 runs（actual data）===\n      random_s42_R1: 0.4604\n      random_s43_R1: 0.4912\n      random_s44_R1: 0.4871\n      random_mean: 0.4796\n      random_std_pp: 1.67\n      embedding_distance_s42_R1: 0.4567\n      # === 预测 runs ===\n      embedding_distance_s43_R1: 0.4880\n      embedding_distance_s44_R1: 0.4830\n      dataflow_aware_s42_R1: 0.4530\n      dataflow_aware_s43_R1: 0.4820\n      dataflow_aware_s44_R1: 0.4780\n      # === 汇总统计 ===\n      embed_mean: 0.4759\n      embed_vs_random_mean_delta_pp: -0.37\n      dataflow_mean: 0.4710\n      dataflow_vs_random_mean_delta_pp: -0.86\n      # === 统计检验 ===\n      embed_vs_random_paired_deltas: [-0.37, -0.32, -0.41]\n      embed_vs_random_bootstrap_95ci: [-0.52, -0.22]\n      embed_vs_random_ci_includes_zero: false\n      dataflow_vs_random_paired_deltas: [-0.74, -0.92, -0.91]\n      dataflow_vs_random_bootstrap_95ci: [-1.02, -0.70]\n      dataflow_vs_random_ci_includes_zero: false\n      starcoder_note: \"Per-encoder CIs exclude zero (embed/dataflow consistently ≤ random), but POOLED cross-encoder CI includes zero\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      StarCoder worst tier 预测：embed 和 dataflow consistently ≤ random。\n\n      embed_s43 预测 0.4880（vs random 0.4912, Δ=-0.32pp）：StarCoder 的 \"healthy\" \n      representation space（pos_sim=0.7985, margin=0.194 for random）意味着 embedding-distance \n      mining 选择的 negatives 过度 hard（neg_sim pushed to 0.741, margin compressed to \n      0.067）。这些 \"too hard\" negatives 导致 training signal noise-dominated，轻微 \n      损害 convergence。\n\n      embed_s44 预测 0.4830（vs random 0.4871, Δ=-0.41pp）：consistent with s42 pattern。\n\n      dataflow_s42-s44 预测一致为 negative delta（-0.74 to -0.92pp）：structural filtering \n      + BM25 ranking 选择的 negatives 在 StarCoder 的 representation space 中既 \n      structurally disconnected 又 lexically similar，但 StarCoder 的 healthy margin \n      已经足够区分——这些 negatives 反而是 \"misleading hard\" rather than \"informative hard\"。\n\n      关键差异 vs Qwen：StarCoder 的 per-encoder CI 可能 exclude zero（all 3 seeds \n      negative），suggesting embed HURTS StarCoder。但 pooled cross-encoder analysis \n      （with Qwen's sign-inconsistent deltas）CI 仍然 includes zero。\n\n      Worst tier narrative interpretation：\n      - Qwen: embed ≈ random（sign-inconsistent，CI includes zero）\n      - StarCoder: embed slightly hurts（consistent negative, CI may exclude zero）\n      - UniXcoder: embed ≈ random（all within 0.37pp）\n      - Cross-encoder pooled: CI includes zero → \"no reliable benefit across architectures\"\n\n      StarCoder embed harm + Qwen embed null = \"mining strategy effect is encoder-dependent \n      but NEVER reliably positive\"。This is worse than \"no effect\" — it's \"unpredictable \n      effect that may be harmful.\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 6: StarCoder2-3B R@1 (best_by_R@1, pool=8)\"\n        columns: [Strategy, s42, s43, s44, \"Mean±Std\", \"Δ vs Random\"]\n        rows:\n          - [random, 0.4604, 0.4912, 0.4871, \"0.4796±0.017\", \"—\"]\n          - [embedding_distance, 0.4567, \"0.4880*\", \"0.4830*\", \"0.4759±0.017\", \"-0.37pp\"]\n          - [dataflow_aware, \"0.4530*\", \"0.4820*\", \"0.4780*\", \"0.4710±0.016\", \"-0.86pp\"]\n        note: \"* = predicted. StarCoder per-encoder CIs may exclude zero (consistent negative deltas), but pooled cross-encoder CI includes zero.\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 6: Qwen vs StarCoder paired delta comparison — showing Qwen sign-inconsistent vs StarCoder consistently negative\"\n    analysis: |\n      StarCoder 结果是 worst tier 中最 damaging 的 evidence：pilot pattern（embed +1.6pp）\n      在 full scale 完全反转为 consistently negative。这一 \"pilot → full scale degradation\" \n      pattern 是 Direction 2（negative result study）的核心叙事支撑。\n\n      与 representation geometry 的关系：StarCoder 的 healthy margin（0.194 for random）\n      被 embed mining 压缩至 0.067，loss of margin diversity 可能是 performance degradation \n      的 mechanism。但在 worst tier 下，这个 mechanism 的 explanatory power 有限——\n      它解释了 WHY embed hurts StarCoder，但不能 prescriptively 告诉 practitioners 何时 \n      mining 会 help。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_014: Temperature Ablation (Full)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Temperature 消融（τ ∈ {0.05, 0.1, 0.2}）\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: \"3 个 temperature × 3 strategies × 3 seeds × Qwen，测试 strategy ranking 的 regime-specificity\"\n    expected_results:\n      # === τ=0.05 ===\n      tau005_random_R1_mean: 0.555\n      tau005_embed_R1_mean: 0.552\n      tau005_embed_vs_random_pp: -0.3\n      tau005_strategy_ranking: \"random ≈ embed ≈ dataflow\"\n      # === τ=0.1 (baseline) ===\n      tau010_note: \"τ=0.07 in actual config, τ=0.1 in plan — using actual τ=0.07 data\"\n      tau010_embed_vs_random_pp: -0.17\n      # === τ=0.2 ===\n      tau020_random_R1_mean: 0.548\n      tau020_embed_R1_mean: 0.546\n      tau020_embed_vs_random_pp: -0.2\n      tau020_strategy_ranking: \"random ≈ embed ≈ dataflow\"\n      # === overall ===\n      strategy_ranking_changes_with_tau: false\n      null_result_regime_independent: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      Worst tier 下 temperature 不影响 strategy ranking（永远都是 null）：\n\n      τ=0.05（sharper distribution）：更强的 gradient signal，但对所有 strategies 等量增强。\n      Absolute R@1 微降（training 不太稳定，容易 overfit），但 strategy delta 仍在 noise \n      floor 内。Embed vs random ≈ -0.3pp（CI includes zero）。\n\n      τ=0.2（smoother distribution）：更弱的 gradient signal，所有 strategies 等量减弱。\n      Absolute R@1 微降（gradient 太弱，学习不充分），strategy delta 仍 ≈ 0。\n\n      关键论据：如果 embed mining 的 advantage 是 regime-specific（仅在 τ=0.05 出现），\n      则 pilot 的 positive result 可以归因于 τ 选择。但 worst tier 下 ALL temperatures \n      都是 null，排除了 \"wrong temperature regime\" 作为 null result 的 explanation。\n\n      这一结果强化 null result 的 robustness：\"mining strategy effect is not hidden in \n      a different temperature regime — it genuinely doesn't exist at this scale.\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S1: Embed−random delta (pp) by temperature\"\n        columns: [\"τ\", \"Δ R@1 (pp)\", \"95% CI\", \"Abs Random R@1\"]\n        rows:\n          - [0.05, \"-0.3\", \"[-1.1, +0.5]\", 0.555]\n          - [0.07, \"-0.17\", \"[-0.92, +0.58]\", 0.570]\n          - [0.2, \"-0.2\", \"[-1.0, +0.6]\", 0.548]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S3: Strategy delta vs temperature curve，showing flat (null) pattern across τ values\"\n    analysis: \"Temperature ablation confirms null result is regime-independent. No τ value rescues mining strategy effectiveness.\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_015: Dynamic Mining Baseline\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Dynamic embedding mining baseline\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_015\"\n    description: \"每 epoch 重新 mine embedding negatives vs static（一次 mine from pretrained），隔离 selection criterion vs curriculum shift\"\n    expected_results:\n      static_embed_R1_mean: 0.568\n      dynamic_embed_R1_mean: 0.567\n      dynamic_vs_static_pp: -0.1\n      dynamic_vs_random_pp: -0.27\n      ci_includes_zero: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      Dynamic mining 与 static mining 无差异：\n\n      Static mining 从 pretrained encoder mine negatives（one-shot）。Dynamic mining \n      每个 epoch 用 updated encoder 重新 mine。如果 static mining 的 problem 是 \n      \"stale negatives\"（encoder 学习后 difficulty ranking 变化），dynamic mining 应该 \n      显著改善。\n\n      Worst tier 下 dynamic ≈ static ≈ random，因为：\n      1. Encoder 在 LoRA fine-tuning 后 representation 变化很小（LoRA rank=16，仅更新 \n         0.5% 参数），difficulty ranking 几乎不变\n      2. 即使 difficulty ranking 更新了，mining 的 marginal value 在 full-scale data \n         下已经为零——更 fresh 的 negatives 不会改变这个 fundamental limitation\n      3. Dynamic mining 的 computational overhead（每 epoch 重新 encode 全 corpus + \n         nearest neighbor search）相当于 ~10% training time，ROI 为零\n\n      这一结果排除了 \"static vs dynamic\" confound 作为 null result 的 explanation。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Dynamic mining doesn't rescue the null. The problem isn't stale negatives — it's that mining signal is fundamentally marginal at full scale.\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_016: Bootstrap CI for SWE-bench\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"SWE-bench Bootstrap CI\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_016\"\n    description: \"为 SWE-bench Lite resolve rate 添加 95% bootstrap CI\"\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"DROPPED — SWE-bench abandoned\"\n      if_computed:\n        R1: 0.04\n        bootstrap_95ci: [0.01, 0.08]\n        note: \"CI confirms OOD failure is real, not sample noise\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      SWE-bench 已被放弃（R@1=0.04 vs BM25=0.2733）。即使计算 bootstrap CI，也只是 \n      确认 OOD failure 是 real（CI [0.01, 0.08] 远低于 BM25 baseline）。\n\n      在 worst tier 论文中不提 SWE-bench。这意味着论文缺少 downstream task evaluation，\n      是一个 acknowledged limitation。RepoBench-R（plan_004）是唯一的 external validation。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"N/A. SWE-bench dropped from paper. External validation relies entirely on RepoBench-R.\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_018: BM25 Negative Baseline (Training Phase)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"BM25 negative baseline 训练\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_018\"\n    description: \"Phase 1 (mining) 已完成，Phase 2: 训练 BM25 negatives × 3 seeds Qwen + 1 seed StarCoder\"\n    expected_results:\n      # === Phase 1 actual data ===\n      phase1_bm25_mining_done: true\n      bm25_vs_embedding_overlap_k50: 0.871\n      bm25_vs_random_overlap_k50: 0.762\n      # === Phase 2 Qwen training predictions ===\n      qwen_bm25_s42_R1: 0.555\n      qwen_bm25_s43_R1: 0.558\n      qwen_bm25_s44_R1: 0.597\n      qwen_bm25_mean: 0.570\n      qwen_bm25_vs_random_mean_pp: +0.03\n      qwen_bm25_vs_random_ci: [-0.55, +0.59]\n      qwen_bm25_ci_includes_zero: true\n      # === Phase 2 StarCoder training predictions ===\n      starcoder_bm25_s42_R1: 0.459\n      starcoder_bm25_vs_random_s42_pp: -0.14\n      # === Cross-strategy comparison ===\n      bm25_vs_embed_qwen_mean_pp: +0.20\n      bm25_vs_embed_starcoder_s42_pp: +0.24\n      bm25_strategy_ranking: \"bm25 ≈ random > embed ≈ dataflow (but all within noise)\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      BM25 ≈ random 是 worst tier 的 critical prediction，devastating for CoCoHaNeRe narrative。\n\n      Phase 1 overlap analysis 已经 foreshadowed this：BM25 和 embedding negatives 87.1% \n      重叠（k=50 level）。在 large repos（200+ files）中 overlap 下降至 29.7%（Jaccard \n      top-7），但这些 repos 中 BM25 和 embedding 选择的 negatives 在 cosine similarity \n      distribution 上仍然高度相似。\n\n      Qwen BM25 训练预测：3 seeds mean Δ = +0.03pp（essentially zero）。BM25 negatives \n      既不 harm（反驳 MVP artifact where BM25-proxy caused -27pp，那是 labeling bug）也不 \n      help（BM25 similarity ≠ embedding difficulty in a way that improves training）。\n\n      StarCoder BM25 预测：Δ = -0.14pp（also ≈ zero）。\n\n      CoCoHaNeRe narrative 失效分析：\n      1. CoCoHaNeRe 声称 gradient-based mining >> non-differentiable embedding mining\n      2. 我们的原始叙事：simple embedding mining provides reliable improvement（反驳 CoCoHaNeRe）\n      3. Worst tier 下：BM25 ≈ embed ≈ random → 所有 non-gradient methods 都 ≈ random\n      4. 但我们也不能说 gradient-based methods 更好（未测试）\n      5. 结论：在我们的 setting 下，mining strategy choice doesn't matter at all，无法对 \n         CoCoHaNeRe 的 gradient-based claim 做有意义的评论\n\n      4-strategy comparison 中的微妙 pattern：bm25 ≈ random > embed ≈ dataflow（numerically, \n      not significantly）。这可能暗示 embed 和 dataflow 的 targeted hard negatives 轻微 \n      有害，而 BM25 的 \"untargeted lexical similarity\" 恰好与 random 等效。但 effect sizes \n      全部在 noise floor 内。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 7: 4-Strategy comparison (Qwen, mean across 3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [Strategy, \"R@1 Mean±Std\", \"Δ vs Random (pp)\", \"95% CI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [random, \"0.570±0.027\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [embedding_distance, \"0.568±0.023\", \"-0.17\", \"[-0.92, +0.58]\"]\n          - [dataflow_aware, \"0.560±0.014\", \"-0.99\", \"[-2.36, +0.58]\"]\n          - [bm25, \"0.570±0.023\", \"+0.03\", \"[-0.55, +0.59]\"]\n        note: \"All 95% CIs include zero. Mining strategy ≈ noise.\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 7: 4-strategy comparison bar chart with error bars，showing all strategies clustered around random baseline\"\n      - \"Fig 8: BM25-embedding negative overlap heatmap by repo size tier，showing 87% overlap at corpus level\"\n    analysis: |\n      BM25 null result 完成了 worst tier 的最后一块拼图：\n\n      4 种 mining strategies（random, embedding, dataflow, bm25）全部 ≈ random。\n      This is not \"embedding is the best non-gradient method\" (original narrative) \n      nor \"BM25 is harmful\" (CoCoHaNeRe narrative) — it's \"nothing matters at this scale.\"\n\n      Paper framing 必须完全 reframe：从 \"which strategy is best\" 转变为 \n      \"why does strategy choice not matter\" + \"what does matter (checkpoint criterion).\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_019: Pool Size Sensitivity\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Pool size sensitivity（pool={50, 100, 200, 500}）\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_019\"\n    description: \"测试 strategy ranking 在 realistic pool sizes 下的稳定性\"\n    expected_results:\n      # === Qwen results by pool size ===\n      qwen_pool_8:\n        random_R1: 0.570\n        embed_R1: 0.568\n        delta_pp: -0.17\n        strategy_ranking: \"random ≈ embed\"\n      qwen_pool_50:\n        random_R1: 0.420\n        embed_R1: 0.415\n        delta_pp: -0.5\n        strategy_ranking: \"random > embed (but CI includes zero)\"\n      qwen_pool_100:\n        random_R1: 0.310\n        embed_R1: 0.308\n        delta_pp: -0.2\n        strategy_ranking: \"indistinguishable\"\n      qwen_pool_200:\n        random_R1: 0.210\n        embed_R1: 0.208\n        delta_pp: -0.2\n        strategy_ranking: \"indistinguishable\"\n      qwen_pool_500:\n        random_R1: 0.115\n        embed_R1: 0.113\n        delta_pp: -0.2\n        strategy_ranking: \"indistinguishable\"\n      # === Pool size effect vs strategy effect ===\n      pool_8_to_500_random_drop_pp: 45.5\n      strategy_delta_at_pool_500_pp: 0.2\n      pool_to_strategy_ratio: \"227x\"\n      ranking_reversal_observed: true\n      ranking_reversal_pool: 50\n      ranking_reversal_note: \"At pool=50, embed vs random delta is -0.5pp (embed worse), while at pool=8 it's -0.17pp. Direction consistent but magnitude varies with pool size.\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Pool size sensitivity 是 worst tier 论文的 decisive evidence。\n\n      Predictions 基于两个 mechanisms：\n      1. Pool size 增大时，absolute R@1 单调下降（更多 distractors → harder retrieval）。\n         Pool=8 → pool=500 的 R@1 drop ≈ 45pp，远超任何 strategy effect。\n      2. Strategy differences 被 proportionally compressed：如果 strategy effect 是 \n         multiplicative（improves relative ranking），larger pool 应该 preserve delta。\n         但如果 effect 是 additive noise（which worst tier assumes），larger pool 中 \n         delta 保持 absolute size 而 relative importance shrinks。\n\n      Worst tier 预测：strategy ranking 在 pool>50 时实质性消失。Pool=50 时 embed \n      已经比 random 差 0.5pp（consistent with pilot data showing -3.7pp at pool=50, \n      but full-scale model is better trained）。Pool=100+ 时 delta 压缩到 <0.3pp。\n\n      ranking_reversal 在 pool=50 观察到：embed vs random 从 pool=8 的 -0.17pp 扩大到 \n      pool=50 的 -0.5pp（negative direction amplified）。这意味着 embed mining 在 \n      larger pools 中的 slight harm 被放大——consistent with \"too hard negatives cause \n      slight overfitting that hurts at realistic retrieval difficulty。\"\n\n      论文 contribution：pool size sensitivity analysis 证明现有 mining strategy 文献的 \n      reported gains（在 pool=5-20 的 tiny val sets 上评估）不 generalize to realistic \n      retrieval scenarios（pool=100-500+）。这是 evaluation methodology warning 的 \n      additional evidence。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 8: Qwen R@1 by pool size (mean across 3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [Pool Size, Random, Embed, Dataflow, \"Embed−Random (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [8, 0.570, 0.568, 0.560, \"-0.17\"]\n          - [50, 0.420, 0.415, 0.408, \"-0.5\"]\n          - [100, 0.310, 0.308, 0.303, \"-0.2\"]\n          - [200, 0.210, 0.208, 0.205, \"-0.2\"]\n          - [500, 0.115, 0.113, 0.111, \"-0.2\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 9 (main): R@1 vs pool size curve for each strategy，showing parallel decline with no strategy separation\"\n      - \"Fig 9 inset: Strategy delta vs pool size，showing delta stays near zero across all pool sizes\"\n    analysis: |\n      Pool size sensitivity 证明 worst tier 的 scale-dependent argument：\n\n      \"Mining strategy evaluations conducted on small validation pools (pool < 20) \n      measure pool-size-dependent retrieval ease, not strategy-dependent improvement. \n      At realistic pool sizes (100+), strategy differences vanish entirely.\"\n\n      Combined with plan_008 (data scaling) and plan_005 (stratification), this forms \n      a comprehensive negative result: mining strategy effect disappears along EVERY \n      scaling dimension (data size, pool size, and subpopulation).\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_020: UniXcoder Multi-seed Validation\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"UniXcoder 多种子验证（s42/s43/s44）\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_020\"\n    description: \"UniXcoder-base (125M, encoder-only) 上 3-strategy × 3-seed 验证 cross-architecture generalization\"\n    expected_results:\n      # === s42 actual ===\n      s42_random_R1: 0.5534\n      s42_embed_R1: 0.5497\n      s42_dataflow_R1: 0.5510\n      s42_strategy_range_pp: 0.37\n      # === s43 predictions ===\n      s43_random_R1: 0.577\n      s43_embed_R1: 0.573\n      s43_dataflow_R1: 0.575\n      s43_strategy_range_pp: 0.4\n      # === s44 predictions ===\n      s44_random_R1: 0.560\n      s44_embed_R1: 0.556\n      s44_dataflow_R1: 0.558\n      s44_strategy_range_pp: 0.4\n      # === cross-seed summary ===\n      random_mean: 0.5635\n      random_std_pp: 1.2\n      embed_mean: 0.5596\n      embed_vs_random_mean_pp: -0.39\n      embed_vs_random_ci: [-0.85, +0.07]\n      embed_vs_random_ci_includes_zero: true\n      dataflow_mean: 0.5613\n      dataflow_vs_random_mean_pp: -0.22\n      cross_seed_std_dominates: true\n      # === cross-architecture synthesis ===\n      three_encoder_null: true\n      architecture_types_tested: [\"encoder-only (UniXcoder 125M)\", \"decoder-only (Qwen 3B)\", \"decoder-only (StarCoder 3B)\"]\n    result_rationale: |\n      UniXcoder 在 worst tier 中提供 3rd architecture confirmation of null result。\n\n      UniXcoder-base（125M, encoder-only, RoBERTa-based）与 Qwen/StarCoder（3B, \n      decoder-only）架构完全不同。如果 mining strategy effect 在 125M encoder-only \n      model 上也是 null，则结论的 generality 大幅增强。\n\n      s42 actual data 已显示 0.37pp 全 range（远小于 noise floor）。Worst tier 预测 \n      s43/s44 同样 null（0.4pp range per seed），cross-seed std（1.2pp）远大于 \n      within-seed strategy delta（<0.4pp）。\n\n      Three-encoder null result 的论证力度：\n      1. UniXcoder 125M (encoder-only): null → 不是模型太小的问题\n      2. Qwen 3B (decoder-only, FIM pretrained): null → 不是 Qwen-specific\n      3. StarCoder 3B (decoder-only, code-specific): embed hurts → 更差\n      \n      Cross-architecture generalization：\"no evidence mining strategy matters at this scale, \n      regardless of architecture choice (encoder-only vs decoder-only), model size (125M \n      vs 3B), and pretraining strategy (masked LM vs FIM vs code-specific).\"\n\n      UniXcoder 的额外价值：它的 pos_sim 接近 Qwen（高 similarity, near-saturated），\n      但架构完全不同。这排除了 \"saturation is decoder-only artifact\" 的 objection。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 9: UniXcoder-base R@1 (best_by_R@1, pool=8)\"\n        columns: [Strategy, s42, s43, s44, \"Mean±Std\", \"Δ vs Random\"]\n        rows:\n          - [random, 0.5534, \"0.577*\", \"0.560*\", \"0.564±0.012\", \"—\"]\n          - [embedding_distance, 0.5497, \"0.573*\", \"0.556*\", \"0.560±0.012\", \"-0.39pp\"]\n          - [dataflow_aware, 0.5510, \"0.575*\", \"0.558*\", \"0.561±0.012\", \"-0.22pp\"]\n        note: \"* = predicted. Strategy range <0.4pp per seed.\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 10: Three-encoder comparison panel — R@1 by strategy for Qwen/StarCoder/UniXcoder with 95% CIs，showing universal null\"\n    analysis: |\n      UniXcoder multi-seed 完成了 cross-architecture validation。三种不同架构 × 三种不同 \n      model sizes × 三种不同 pretraining strategies 全部显示 null result。\n\n      This level of consistency across architectures is actually a STRONG finding — \n      it's just a negative one. The paper can claim: \"We provide the most comprehensive \n      evidence to date that hard negative mining strategies do not reliably improve \n      contrastive code retrieval at training scales of 10K+ instances.\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_021: Temperature Ablation (Reduced)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Temperature 消融（reduced scope: τ={0.05, 0.2} × random+embed × Qwen × s42）\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_021\"\n    description: \"Reduced scope of plan_014: 4 runs total to verify regime-specificity\"\n    expected_results:\n      tau005_random_s42_R1: 0.548\n      tau005_embed_s42_R1: 0.545\n      tau005_delta_pp: -0.3\n      tau020_random_s42_R1: 0.540\n      tau020_embed_s42_R1: 0.538\n      tau020_delta_pp: -0.2\n      regime_specificity_confirmed: false\n      null_at_all_temperatures: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      Reduced scope 足以 falsify \"τ=0.07 是 null 的原因\" 假说。\n\n      两个极端温度（0.05 sharp, 0.2 smooth）都显示 embed ≈ random（delta -0.2 to -0.3pp）。\n      Strategy ranking 不随 τ 变化。Absolute R@1 在极端 τ 时微降（training less optimal），\n      但 relative strategy performance 保持 null。\n\n      4 runs（15h GPU）足以 rule out regime-specificity concern。Full plan_014（70h）\n      在 worst tier 下 not justified — 已知 null result 是 regime-independent。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Minimal evidence needed to rule out temperature regime as explanation for null result.\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Additional worst-tier required experiments (not in current plan)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"额外 seeds 确认 null（5-10 seeds）\"\n    plan_id: \"worst_extra_a\"\n    description: \"在 Qwen 上扩展至 5-10 seeds（embed + random），power analysis 确认需要多少 seeds 才能 detect 0.3pp effect\"\n    expected_results:\n      seeds_5_embed_vs_random_mean_pp: -0.10\n      seeds_5_ci: [-0.45, +0.25]\n      seeds_5_ci_includes_zero: true\n      seeds_10_embed_vs_random_mean_pp: -0.08\n      seeds_10_ci: [-0.30, +0.14]\n      seeds_10_ci_includes_zero: true\n      power_analysis:\n        detectable_effect_at_80_power_3seeds_pp: 2.5\n        detectable_effect_at_80_power_5seeds_pp: 1.5\n        detectable_effect_at_80_power_10seeds_pp: 0.8\n        seeds_needed_for_0.3pp_effect: \">50\"\n        conclusion: \"Even 10 seeds cannot reliably detect 0.3pp effects given cross-seed std of 2.7pp\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Power analysis 揭示 fundamental limitation：with cross-seed std ≈ 2.7pp，detecting \n      a 0.3pp effect at 80% power requires >50 seeds（paired t-test, α=0.05）。\n\n      扩展至 5-10 seeds 不会改变 conclusion（CI 仍 includes zero），但会 sharpen the \n      null：从 \"can't detect\" 到 \"can confidently bound effect < 0.8pp\"。\n\n      这也成为 methodological contribution：prior work reporting 1-2pp gains from mining \n      strategies with 1-3 seeds is statistically inadequate. Our power analysis shows \n      minimum 10 seeds needed to detect effects in the 1pp range for this task。\n\n      Worst tier 论文 should include this power analysis as Table in methodology section。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 10: Power analysis for strategy effect detection\"\n        columns: [Seeds, \"Detectable Effect (pp, 80% power)\", \"Estimated 95% CI width (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [3, 2.5, 2.9]\n          - [5, 1.5, 2.2]\n          - [10, 0.8, 1.5]\n          - [50, 0.3, 0.7]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: |\n      Power analysis 是 worst tier 论文（Direction 1: Methodology Warning）的 key table。\n      它直接挑战 prior work 的 statistical adequacy，属于 community-level methodological \n      contribution，不依赖于我们自己的 positive findings。\n\n  - name: \"Scaling analysis（data size vs strategy effect）\"\n    plan_id: \"worst_extra_b\"\n    description: \"Same as plan_008 but framed as worst tier's required additional experiment\"\n    expected_results:\n      note: \"See plan_008 predictions above — same experiment\"\n    result_rationale: \"Already covered under plan_008. Required for Direction 2 (negative result study) core figure.\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Cross-reference with plan_008.\"\n\n  - name: \"Published mining paper reproduction attempt\"\n    plan_id: \"worst_extra_c\"\n    description: \"Attempt to reproduce 1-2 published hard negative mining papers' claims in our setting\"\n    expected_results:\n      paper_1_name: \"CoCoHaNeRe (TOSEM 2025)\"\n      paper_1_claimed_gain_pp: 3.5\n      paper_1_reproduced_gain_pp: 0.2\n      paper_1_reproduced_ci: [-0.8, +1.2]\n      paper_1_reproduced_significant: false\n      paper_2_name: \"ANCE (ICLR 2021)\"\n      paper_2_claimed_gain_pp: 2.8\n      paper_2_reproduced_gain_pp: 0.4\n      paper_2_reproduced_ci: [-0.5, +1.3]\n      paper_2_reproduced_significant: false\n      reproduction_conclusion: \"Neither paper's claimed gains replicate in our controlled setting with multi-seed CIs\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Reproduction attempt 在 worst tier 下会失败：prior work 的 reported gains 在我们的 \n      controlled setting（multi-seed, fixed pool, proper CI）下不 replicate。\n\n      可能原因：\n      1. Prior work 使用 single seed + cherry-picked checkpoint（our D062 finding）\n      2. Prior work 评估在 small pools（our plan_019 finding）\n      3. Prior work 数据规模更小（our plan_008 finding）\n      4. Prior work 使用不同 base models（但 UniXcoder null 表明 architecture isn't the issue）\n\n      Reproduction failure 为 worst tier 论文提供 strongest possible evidence：不仅我们的 \n      mining strategies 无效，prior work 声称有效的 strategies 在 properly controlled \n      setting 下也无效。\n\n      这一 experiment 把 worst tier 论文从 \"our specific methods don't work\" 提升为 \n      \"the field's claims about mining effectiveness may be statistical artifacts\"——\n      这是 EMNLP Main 级别的 contribution。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: |\n      Reproduction attempt 是 worst tier 论文最有野心的 contribution。如果成功证明 \n      prior work 不 replicate，论文变成对整个 hard negative mining 文献的 meta-methodological \n      critique，与 \"checkpoint criterion > mining strategy\" 主题完美呼应。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Checkpoint Criterion Effect (D062) — Core Worst Tier Finding\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Checkpoint selection criterion effect 综合分析\"\n    plan_id: \"D062_synthesis\"\n    description: \"量化 checkpoint 选择标准（best_by_R@1 vs best_by_val_loss）在完整 4-strategy × 3-seed × 3-encoder 矩阵中造成的报告差异\"\n    expected_results:\n      # === Per-run criterion divergence ===\n      per_run_R1_gap_mean_pp: 1.3\n      per_run_R1_gap_max_pp: 2.0\n      per_run_R1_gap_min_pp: 0.0\n      runs_where_criteria_pick_different_step: \"12/18 (67%)\"\n      # === Strategy ranking affected by criterion ===\n      ranking_flips_by_criterion: 3\n      ranking_flip_example: \"Qwen s44: by R@1 → random best; by val_loss → random best (same); but Qwen s43: by R@1 → embed best; by val_loss → random best (flip)\"\n      # === Combined methodological variance ===\n      total_analyst_flexibility_pp: 15.2\n      composed_of:\n        checkpoint_criterion_contribution_pp: 3.5\n        seed_selection_contribution_pp: 5.0\n        pool_size_contribution_pp: 6.7\n      strategy_effect_in_context_pp: 0.5\n      methodology_to_strategy_ratio: \"30x\"\n      # === Robust checkpoint effect (the surviving finding) ===\n      checkpoint_criterion_effect_pp: 14.8\n      checkpoint_criterion_robust_across_seeds: true\n      checkpoint_criterion_robust_across_encoders: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      D062 checkpoint criterion effect 是 worst tier 唯一幸存的核心发现。\n\n      effect 的构成（~15pp total analyst flexibility）：\n      1. Checkpoint 选择标准（3.5pp）：同一个 run 中，best_by_R@1 checkpoint 的 R@1 比 \n         best_by_val_loss checkpoint 的 R@1 高 0-2pp（mean 1.3pp）。67% 的 runs 中两个 \n         criteria 选择不同的 checkpoint。在 3 strategies × 3 seeds matrix 中，这会导致 \n         strategy ranking flip（3 次 observed）。\n      2. Seed 选择（5.0pp）：Qwen random cross-seed range = 0.5527-0.6009 = 4.82pp。\n         Cherry-picking best vs worst seed 造成 ~5pp 报告差异。\n      3. Pool size（6.7pp）：从 val pool=8 到 realistic pool=50，R@1 下降 ~15pp；\n         但 relative strategy ranking 可能 flip（pilot 中 embed 在 pool=8 好但 pool=50 差）。\n         Pool size 选择在论文中通常不报告，是 hidden methodology choice。\n\n      Strategy effect（0.5pp）在这 15pp analyst flexibility space 中仅占 3.3%。\n\n      这一分析的论证力度：不是说研究者会恶意 cherry-pick，而是说在 standard practice 中\n      （选 best checkpoint，选 best seed for reporting，使用 convenient pool size for eval），\n      methodological choices 的 variance 远远大于 effect being studied。This is a genuine \n      methodological contribution that doesn't depend on our specific mining strategies。\n\n      Robustness：checkpoint criterion effect 在 all 3 encoders × all 3 seeds 上一致 \n      存在（val_loss-best 和 R@1-best 经常 diverge），不是 encoder-specific 或 seed-specific。\n      这使它成为 generalizable finding，适合 EMNLP Main 发表。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 11: Checkpoint criterion effect — R@1 gap between best_by_R@1 and best_by_val_loss checkpoint\"\n        columns: [Encoder, Strategy, Seed, \"R@1 (best_by_R@1)\", \"R@1 (best_by_val_loss)\", \"Gap (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [Qwen, random, s42, 0.5527, 0.5527, 0.0]\n          - [Qwen, random, s43, 0.5554, 0.5357, +1.97]\n          - [Qwen, random, s44, 0.6009, 0.6009, 0.0]\n          - [Qwen, embed, s43, 0.5606, 0.5446, +1.60]\n          - [Qwen, embed, s44, 0.5942, 0.5813, +1.29]\n          - [\"StarCoder*\", random, s42, 0.4604, 0.4537, +0.67]\n          - [\"StarCoder*\", random, s43, 0.4912, 0.4912, 0.0]\n          - [\"StarCoder*\", random, s44, 0.4871, 0.4848, +0.23]\n        note: \"Mean gap: 0.72pp per run. 5/8 runs show criterion divergence. * = actual data for completed runs.\"\n      - name: \"Table 12: Analyst flexibility decomposition\"\n        columns: [Source, \"Variance (pp)\", \"% of total\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Checkpoint criterion (R@1 vs val_loss)\", 3.5, \"23%\"]\n          - [\"Seed selection (best vs worst)\", 5.0, \"33%\"]\n          - [\"Pool size (val pool=8 vs realistic pool=50+)\", 6.7, \"44%\"]\n          - [\"TOTAL methodology variance\", 15.2, \"100%\"]\n          - [\"Mining strategy effect\", 0.5, \"3.3% of methodology variance\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 11 (main): Paired plot showing R@1 at best_by_R@1 vs best_by_val_loss checkpoint for each run，connected by lines showing criterion divergence\"\n      - \"Fig 12: Variance decomposition pie chart — methodology (96.7%) vs strategy (3.3%)\"\n    analysis: |\n      D062 synthesis 提供了 worst tier 论文的 central message：\n\n      \"In contrastive code retrieval, methodological choices in checkpoint selection, \n      seed reporting, and evaluation pool size create 30x more variance in reported \n      results than the mining strategy choice being studied. Before the field can make \n      reliable claims about mining strategy effectiveness, evaluation methodology \n      must be standardized.\"\n\n      这是一个 strong EMNLP Main contribution because：\n      1. It's quantitative (15.2pp vs 0.5pp)\n      2. It generalizes beyond code (applies to any contrastive learning with checkpoint selection)\n      3. It's actionable (researchers can adopt our proposed evaluation protocol)\n      4. It explains prior contradictions in mining literature (different papers use different \n         checkpoint criteria, seeds, pool sizes → conflicting conclusions)\n\n      建议的 evaluation protocol（论文 Section 5 contribution）：\n      - 最少 5 seeds（power analysis shows 3 is inadequate）\n      - Report both best_by_R@1 and best_by_val_loss checkpoints\n      - Evaluate at multiple pool sizes（at least pool=50 and pool=200）\n      - Use paired within-seed comparisons with cluster bootstrap CIs\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4789,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12345,"cache_read_input_tokens":38135,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12345},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e9214298-f5a6-4448-a682-aa14a7b561f2","uuid":"14bc7d82-2701-41ad-8646-b4a6a1efa222"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":1031345,"duration_api_ms":1032165,"num_turns":5,"result":"Now I have all the grounding data. Let me compute the complete worst-tier predictions.\n\nKey observed facts for calibration:\n- Qwen random: mean=0.5697, std=2.71pp across 3 seeds\n- Qwen embed s43/s44 within-seed deltas: +0.52pp, -0.67pp (sign-inconsistent)\n- StarCoder random: mean=0.4796, std=1.67pp; embed_s42=0.4567 (Δ=-0.37pp, already sign-negative)\n- UniXcoder s42: 0.37pp total range across 3 strategies (null)\n- Seed variance 4.6x larger than strategy effect\n- SWE-bench: R@1=0.04 (OOD failure confirmed)\n- BM25-embed overlap: 87% at k=50\n\n```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: |\n  Mining strategy effect indistinguishable from noise at full scale. Cross-seed variance (2-5pp) is 4-10x larger than within-seed strategy delta (<0.5pp). No strategy reliably outperforms random across encoders. Only surviving contribution: checkpoint selection criterion (R@1 vs val_loss) causes 10-18pp reported performance variation, dwarfing any mining strategy effect.\n\n  完全 reframe 为以下两个方向之一（仍冲 EMNLP Main）：\n  方向 1 — \"Checkpoint Selection Criterion Matters More Than Mining Strategy for Code Retrieval\"\n    核心贡献 = methodological finding：在 controlled 4-strategy × 3-seed × 3-encoder 实验中，checkpoint 选择标准造成 +10-18pp 报告差异，mining strategy 贡献 <0.5pp。Evaluation methodology warning for contrastive code retrieval community。\n  方向 2 — \"Why Hard Negative Mining Doesn't Scale for Code Retrieval: A Negative Result Study\"\n    Pilot → full scale degradation pattern 本身作为贡献：(a) full-scale random baseline 更强（naturally hard negatives 更多）；(b) pretrained decoder-only encoder 的 representation quality 使 mining signal marginal；(c) 3 seeds × 3 encoders 均确认 null。\n\n  必须额外做：(a) 5-10 seeds 确认 null；(b) data size scaling analysis（1K vs 3K vs 5K vs 11K）；(c) 1-2 个 published mining paper 的 reproduction attempt。\n\n  BM25 ≈ random 使 CoCoHaNeRe 纠正叙事失效 — 既无法说 BM25 害人，也无法说 embedding 救人。整个 mining strategy 维度在此 scale 下坍缩为 noise。\n\n  CodeQL pipeline 保留为 practical contribution + representation geometry analysis 保留为 explanatory tool（解释 WHY strategies fail to differentiate）。UniXcoder null 成为 corroborating evidence。SWE-bench 不提（OOD failure，R@1=0.04）。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_001: M1 CodeQL Extraction (DONE)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"M1 全量 CodeQL 提取\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_001\"\n    description: \"5K SWE-smith repos data-flow extraction + connected vs gold statistics\"\n    expected_results:\n      status: DONE\n      structural_data_rate: 0.36\n      repos_with_output: 123\n      zero_timeout_rate: true\n      z_pct_mean: 0.78\n    result_rationale: |\n      基础设施实验，结果与 tier 无关。CodeQL pipeline 在 worst tier 下保留为 practical contribution：\n      0% timeout、78% connected-not-gold rate、123/131 repo coverage 证明 scope-bounded \n      inter-procedural data-flow analysis 在工业级 codebase 上可行。这是 reframe 后论文的\n      supporting methodology 贡献，不受 mining strategy null result 影响。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"不受 tier 影响。作为 reframe 后论文的 Section 3 (Methodology) 支撑。\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_002: M2 Full Qwen Training (remaining runs)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"M2 全量 Qwen 4-strategy × 3-seed 训练\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_002\"\n    description: \"Qwen2.5-Coder-3B LoRA: random/embed/dataflow/bm25 × seeds 42/43/44。6 runs 已完成（random ×3, embed s43/s44, dataflow s43），预测剩余 6 runs。\"\n    expected_results:\n      # === 已完成 runs（actual data）===\n      random_s42_R1: 0.5527\n      random_s43_R1: 0.5554\n      random_s44_R1: 0.6009\n      random_mean: 0.5697\n      random_std_pp: 2.71\n      embedding_distance_s43_R1: 0.5606\n      embedding_distance_s44_R1: 0.5942\n      dataflow_aware_s43_R1: 0.5564\n      # === 预测 runs ===\n      embedding_distance_s42_R1: 0.549\n      dataflow_aware_s42_R1: 0.548\n      dataflow_aware_s44_R1: 0.575\n      bm25_s42_R1: 0.555\n      bm25_s43_R1: 0.558\n      bm25_s44_R1: 0.597\n      # === 汇总统计 ===\n      embed_mean: 0.568\n      embed_std_pp: 2.3\n      embed_vs_random_mean_delta_pp: -0.17\n      dataflow_mean: 0.560\n      dataflow_std_pp: 1.4\n      dataflow_vs_random_mean_delta_pp: -0.99\n      bm25_mean: 0.570\n      bm25_std_pp: 2.3\n      bm25_vs_random_mean_delta_pp: +0.03\n      # === 统计检验 ===\n      embed_vs_random_paired_deltas: [-0.37, +0.52, -0.67]\n      embed_vs_random_bootstrap_95ci: [-0.92, +0.58]\n      embed_vs_random_ci_includes_zero: true\n      dataflow_vs_random_paired_deltas: [-0.47, +0.10, -2.59]\n      dataflow_vs_random_bootstrap_95ci: [-2.36, +0.58]\n      dataflow_vs_random_ci_includes_zero: true\n      bm25_vs_random_paired_deltas: [+0.23, +0.26, -0.39]\n      bm25_vs_random_bootstrap_95ci: [-0.55, +0.59]\n      bm25_vs_random_ci_includes_zero: true\n      cross_seed_std_dominates_strategy: true\n      seed_noise_to_strategy_ratio: 4.6\n    result_rationale: |\n      Worst tier 核心预测：all 3 mining strategies 与 random 不可区分。\n\n      embed_s42 预测 0.549（略低于 random 0.5527）：s42 使用 3-epoch regime（无 early stopping），\n      更长训练使 embed 的 hard negatives 导致轻微 overfitting。Qwen pos_sim=0.9855（saturated），\n      embedding-distance negatives 选自同一 cosine cone 内的样本，与 random 自然产生的 hard \n      negatives 信息量相当。s42 已有的 embed pilot（0.5557）在 pool=8 val set 上显示 +2pp，\n      但 full-scale training data 使 random baseline 足够强，消除了 marginal advantage。\n\n      dataflow_s42 预测 0.548：structural filtering 在 full-scale data 中被稀释。34% \n      structural data rate 意味着 66% 的 query 回退到 BM25-based selection，structural \n      signal 被 fallback noise 淹没。full-scale random 已包含足够 naturally hard negatives，\n      dataflow filtering 无法提供额外区分度。\n\n      dataflow_s44 预测 0.575（vs random 0.6009 = -2.59pp）：s44 的 val split 系统性偏易\n      （所有策略 R@1 更高），但 random s44 异常获益更多——可能因为 easy split 中 random \n      negatives 恰好足够 hard（pool 刚好困难度适中），而 dataflow 的 structural filtering \n      反而排除了一些有用的 borderline negatives。\n\n      bm25 ≈ random（+0.03pp mean）：BM25 overlap 分析已显示 bm25 与 embedding negatives \n      87.1% 重叠（k=50 level）。在 full-scale training 中，BM25-selected negatives 与 \n      random sampling 的差异被大量训练数据的多样性所稀释。BM25 既不 harm（反驳 MVP \n      artifact）也不 help（mining strategy 维度在此 scale 下无效）。\n\n      关键统计论证：cross-seed std（2.71pp for random）是 within-seed strategy delta \n      mean_abs（0.59pp for embed）的 4.6 倍。3 seeds 的 bootstrap 95% CI 全部包含零。\n      结论：在 n=3 seeds 下，无法拒绝 \"mining strategy effect = 0\" 的零假设。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Qwen2.5-Coder-3B R@1 (best_by_R@1, pool=8)\"\n        columns: [Strategy, s42, s43, s44, \"Mean±Std\", \"Δ vs Random\"]\n        rows:\n          - [random, 0.5527, 0.5554, 0.6009, \"0.5697±0.027\", \"—\"]\n          - [embedding_distance, \"0.549*\", 0.5606, 0.5942, \"0.568±0.023\", \"-0.17pp\"]\n          - [dataflow_aware, \"0.548*\", 0.5564, \"0.575*\", \"0.560±0.014\", \"-0.99pp\"]\n          - [bm25, \"0.555*\", \"0.558*\", \"0.597*\", \"0.570±0.023\", \"+0.03pp\"]\n        note: \"* = predicted. All strategy vs random 95% CIs include zero.\"\n      - name: \"Table 2: Paired within-seed strategy deltas (pp)\"\n        columns: [Comparison, s42, s43, s44, Mean, \"95% CI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"embed−random\", \"-0.37\", \"+0.52\", \"-0.67\", \"-0.17\", \"[-0.92, +0.58]\"]\n          - [\"dataflow−random\", \"-0.47\", \"+0.10\", \"-2.59\", \"-0.99\", \"[-2.36, +0.58]\"]\n          - [\"bm25−random\", \"+0.23\", \"+0.26\", \"-0.39\", \"+0.03\", \"[-0.55, +0.59]\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 1a: Paired delta plot — within-seed embed−random 和 dataflow−random deltas with 95% bootstrap CIs，显示所有 CI 跨越零线\"\n      - \"Fig 1b: Seed vs Strategy variance decomposition bar chart — cross-seed std (2.71pp) vs mean strategy delta (<0.5pp)，显示 seed 主导\"\n    analysis: |\n      Qwen 全量训练结果确认 mining strategy effect 在此 scale 下为 noise。\n      3 个核心发现：\n      1. Embed vs random sign-inconsistent across seeds（s43 正, s42/s44 负）→ 不可靠\n      2. Dataflow 因 fallback dilution（66% 无 structural data）+ natural random hardness \n         而系统性略低于 random\n      3. BM25 ≈ random，排除了 CoCoHaNeRe narrative（BM25 既不害人也不帮人）\n\n      Cross-seed std 4.6x > strategy effect：paired within-seed comparison 是唯一\n      合理的分析方法，但即使 paired 后，CI 仍包含零。\n\n      Checkpoint criterion divergence 贡献更大发现：s43 的 val_loss-best（step 500, \n      R@1=0.5357）和 R@1-best（step 1500, R@1=0.5554）差 1.97pp，是 strategy effect 的 \n      3.3 倍。此 methodological finding 成为 worst tier 论文的核心贡献。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_003: SWE-bench Lite Evaluation (DONE, failed)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"SWE-bench Lite end-to-end 评估\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003\"\n    description: \"3 strategies × best checkpoint on SWE-bench Lite 300 instances\"\n    expected_results:\n      status: DONE_FAILED\n      random_s42_R1: 0.04\n      random_s42_R5: 0.11\n      random_s42_R10: 0.14\n      bm25_baseline_R1: 0.2733\n      delta_vs_bm25: -23.33\n      note: \"Neural retriever OOD 泛化完全失败，已放弃\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      SWE-bench 使用 12 个 popular Python repos，与 SWE-smith 5K repos 的分布完全不同。\n      Contrastive model 在 SWE-smith 内部验证集上 R@1=0.55，但 OOD 场景下坍缩至 0.04，\n      远低于 BM25 baseline（0.2733）。\n\n      Worst tier 下此结果强化了 negative narrative：\n      1. 即使 mining strategy 在 in-distribution 上有微小差异，OOD 场景下完全不保留\n      2. 无法做 downstream task evaluation，缺少 extrinsic validation\n      3. Reviewer 会指出：如果 retriever 连 BM25 都不如，mining strategy 的讨论毫无意义\n      \n      Director decision：放弃 SWE-bench，不再重跑。外部验证改用 RepoBench-R（plan_004）。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"SWE-bench 在 worst tier 论文中不提。OOD failure 是已知局限但不影响 in-distribution methodology contribution。\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_004: RepoBench-R Cross-file Retrieval\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"RepoBench-R cross-file retrieval 评估\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: \"Retrieval-only evaluation on RepoBench-R test_easy (pool~6) 和 test_hard (pool~18)，3 strategies × 3 seeds × 2 encoders with 95% CIs\"\n    expected_results:\n      # === Qwen test_easy (pool~6) ===\n      qwen_easy_random_R1_mean: 0.875\n      qwen_easy_embed_R1_mean: 0.870\n      qwen_easy_dataflow_R1_mean: 0.868\n      qwen_easy_strategy_range_pp: 0.7\n      # === Qwen test_hard (pool~18) ===\n      qwen_hard_random_R1_mean: 0.510\n      qwen_hard_embed_R1_mean: 0.507\n      qwen_hard_dataflow_R1_mean: 0.503\n      qwen_hard_strategy_range_pp: 0.7\n      # === StarCoder test_easy ===\n      starcoder_easy_random_R1_mean: 0.820\n      starcoder_easy_embed_R1_mean: 0.815\n      starcoder_easy_dataflow_R1_mean: 0.810\n      starcoder_easy_strategy_range_pp: 1.0\n      # === StarCoder test_hard ===\n      starcoder_hard_random_R1_mean: 0.430\n      starcoder_hard_embed_R1_mean: 0.425\n      starcoder_hard_dataflow_R1_mean: 0.418\n      starcoder_hard_strategy_range_pp: 1.2\n      # === 统计 ===\n      pool_size_effect_easy_vs_hard_pp: 36.5\n      strategy_effect_within_pool_pp: \"<1.2\"\n      pool_dominates_strategy_ratio: \">30x\"\n      all_95ci_include_zero: true\n      repobench_embed_vs_random_mean_pp: -0.35\n    result_rationale: |\n      RepoBench-R 的 pool size effect 完全吞没 strategy effect：\n\n      test_easy（pool~6）：接近 ceiling（R@1 > 0.82），所有策略 ≈ 同等表现。Pool 太小，\n      即使是 random-trained model 也能在 6 个候选中找到正确答案。策略差异 <1pp，不可检测。\n\n      test_hard（pool~18）：R@1 降至 0.42-0.51，但策略排序仍不稳定。Pool=18 相比 \n      SWE-smith val pool=8 更大，但仍不足以放大 <0.5pp 的策略差异。\n\n      关键论据：pool size 从 6→18 造成 R@1 下降 ~36.5pp（Qwen），而策略差异 <1.2pp。\n      Pool size effect 是 strategy effect 的 30x+。这直接支持 worst tier narrative：\n      \"任何声称 mining strategy 有效的实验都必须控制 pool size，否则 reported effect \n      可能完全是 pool size artifact。\"\n\n      Cross-seed 95% CI 全部包含零，确认 SWE-smith 上的 null result 在 RepoBench-R \n      上同样成立。RepoBench-R 无法作为 positive external validation——只能作为额外的 \n      null evidence。\n\n      对 worst tier 论文的影响：RepoBench-R 从 \"corroborating second benchmark\" 变为 \n      \"additional evidence for null result\"。论文可以说 \"Our null finding generalizes \n      beyond SWE-smith to RepoBench-R cross-file retrieval.\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: RepoBench-R R@1 (Qwen, mean±std across 3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [Strategy, \"test_easy (pool~6)\", \"test_hard (pool~18)\", \"Δ (easy−hard)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [random, \"0.875±0.015\", \"0.510±0.020\", \"36.5pp\"]\n          - [embedding_distance, \"0.870±0.014\", \"0.507±0.019\", \"36.3pp\"]\n          - [dataflow_aware, \"0.868±0.016\", \"0.503±0.021\", \"36.5pp\"]\n        note: \"Pool size effect (~36pp) >> strategy effect (<1pp)\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 2: Grouped bar chart — R@1 by strategy for test_easy vs test_hard，error bars showing 95% CI，视觉证明 pool size 主导\"\n    analysis: |\n      RepoBench-R 确认 null result 的 external validity。Pool size effect (36pp) 完全\n      吞没 strategy effect (<1.2pp)，比 SWE-smith pool=8 上的 null 更进一步证明：\n      当 pool size 增大时，strategy 差异不仅不放大反而被压缩。\n\n      这一发现直接支撑 plan_019 的 pool size sensitivity analysis，共同构成 worst tier \n      论文的重要论据：mining strategy effect 是 scale-dependent artifact，在 realistic \n      pool sizes 下完全消失。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_005: Stratified Analysis\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Embedding vs random 深度分层分析\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: \"按 5 个维度分层：repo size / pool size / query-pos similarity / structural data availability / neg_difficulty quartile\"\n    expected_results:\n      # === Stratum 1: repo size ===\n      small_lt50_embed_vs_random_pp: +0.3\n      medium_50_200_embed_vs_random_pp: -0.2\n      large_200_500_embed_vs_random_pp: -0.4\n      xlarge_500plus_embed_vs_random_pp: -0.1\n      repo_size_trend: \"no monotonic pattern\"\n      # === Stratum 2: structural data availability ===\n      rich_dataflow_embed_vs_random_pp: -0.5\n      no_dataflow_embed_vs_random_pp: -0.1\n      confound_note: \"rich_dataflow 99.3% in large/xlarge repos — cannot isolate\"\n      # === Stratum 3: neg_difficulty quartile ===\n      q1_easiest_embed_vs_random_pp: +0.2\n      q2_embed_vs_random_pp: -0.3\n      q3_embed_vs_random_pp: -0.1\n      q4_hardest_embed_vs_random_pp: -0.2\n      difficulty_trend: \"no monotonic relationship\"\n      # === Stratum 4: pool size ===\n      small_pool_embed_vs_random_pp: +0.4\n      large_pool_embed_vs_random_pp: -0.3\n      pool_size_confounded_with_repo: true\n      # === Stratum 5: query-positive similarity ===\n      high_sim_embed_vs_random_pp: -0.3\n      low_sim_embed_vs_random_pp: +0.1\n      # === 总体 ===\n      any_stratum_significant: false\n      all_ci_include_zero: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      Worst tier 下分层分析的核心发现：没有任何 stratum 显示 consistent strategy advantage。\n\n      repo size 分层无单调趋势：small repos 中 embed 微正（+0.3pp），是因为 pool size \n      小时 mining signal 偶然有效；但 medium 和 large repos 中 embed 微负，因为 full-scale \n      random baseline 已足够强。这些差异全部在 noise floor 内（CI 跨越零）。\n\n      structural data availability 分层被 confound 污染：99.3% 的 rich-dataflow instances \n      来自 large/xlarge repos，small repos 中完全不存在。无法隔离 dataflow richness 的\n      独立效应——observed pattern 完全可能是 repo size effect。\n\n      neg_difficulty quartile 分析无单调关系：如果 mining strategy 通过 difficulty \n      gradient 帮助学习，Q4（hardest negatives）应显示最大 improvement。但 worst tier 下 \n      Q4 反而微负（-0.2pp），Q1（easiest）微正（+0.2pp）——完全 inconsistent with \n      difficulty gradient hypothesis。\n\n      所有分层的 CI 均包含零。结论：不存在任何 subpopulation 中 mining strategy \n      consistently helps。Null result 是 uniform，不是被 averaging 掩盖的 heterogeneous \n      effect。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 4: Stratified embed−random delta (pp, Qwen mean across seeds)\"\n        columns: [Stratum, \"Δ R@1 (pp)\", \"95% CI\", N]\n        rows:\n          - [\"small (<50 files)\", \"+0.3\", \"[-1.2, +1.8]\", \"~500\"]\n          - [\"medium (50-200)\", \"-0.2\", \"[-1.4, +1.0]\", \"~4000\"]\n          - [\"large (200-500)\", \"-0.4\", \"[-1.6, +0.8]\", \"~13600\"]\n          - [\"xlarge (500+)\", \"-0.1\", \"[-0.9, +0.7]\", \"~26000\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 3: Stratified delta forest plot — embed−random delta by stratum with 95% CIs，所有 CI 跨越零线\"\n      - \"Fig 4: Heatmap of dataflow richness × repo size cross-tabulation，显示 99.3% confound\"\n    analysis: |\n      分层分析排除了 \"null result is caused by heterogeneous effects averaging out\" \n      的可能性。每个 stratum 单独看都是 null，不存在隐藏的 positive subgroup。\n\n      neg_difficulty quartile 分析进一步动摇了 hard negative mining 的理论基础：\n      if difficulty gradient doesn't monotonically predict improvement，then the entire \n      premise of \"harder negatives → better learning\" is questionable at this scale。\n\n      structural data confound（99.3% in large repos）意味着即使 dataflow strategy \n      在某个 stratum 有微弱优势，也无法归因于 structural information 本身，可能仅是 \n      repo size effect。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_007: Hop Depth Ablation\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"1-hop vs 2-hop vs 3-hop call-graph bounding 消融\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: \"比较不同 call-graph hop depth 对 dataflow-aware mining 的影响\"\n    expected_results:\n      hop1_R1_mean: 0.559\n      hop2_R1_mean: 0.560\n      hop3_R1_mean: 0.558\n      hop_range_pp: 0.2\n      all_vs_random_ci_include_zero: true\n      trend: \"no significant effect of hop depth\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Worst tier 下 hop depth 无效，因为 dataflow-aware strategy 本身就 ≈ random。\n      改变 structural filtering 的粒度（1-hop vs 3-hop）不会改变一个本质上无效策略的效果。\n\n      1-hop 和 3-hop 的区别是 connected file set 的大小：1-hop 更保守（fewer connected \n      files → more candidate negatives），3-hop 更激进（more connected files → fewer \n      candidate negatives）。但在 worst tier 下，无论怎么划分 connected vs disconnected，\n      最终选出的 negatives 与 random 相比都不提供额外 training signal。\n\n      原因：pretrained Qwen geometry 已 saturated（pos_sim=0.9855），negatives 的 structural \n      provenance 不影响 cosine similarity gradient。模型在 embedding space 中看不出 \n      structurally-connected 和 disconnected files 的区别。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S1: Bar chart — R@1 by hop depth (1/2/3) with error bars，显示 flat pattern\"\n    analysis: \"支持 worst tier narrative：structural signal 在 pretrained geometry saturated 时无法提供额外 training gradient。\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_008: Training Data Size Scaling\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"训练数据规模 scaling（1K/3K/5K/11K instances）\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: \"比较不同数据规模下 strategy ranking 是否变化\"\n    expected_results:\n      # === embed−random delta at each scale ===\n      scale_1K_embed_vs_random_pp: +1.2\n      scale_3K_embed_vs_random_pp: +0.5\n      scale_5K_embed_vs_random_pp: +0.2\n      scale_11K_embed_vs_random_pp: -0.17\n      # === trend ===\n      delta_trend: \"monotonically decreasing\"\n      delta_hits_zero_at: \"~4K instances\"\n      pilot_vs_full_degradation_explained: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      这是 worst tier 论文（方向 2: negative result study）的核心 figure。\n\n      Scaling analysis 预测：embed−random delta 随 data size 单调递减，在 ~4K instances \n      处穿越零线。这解释了 pilot（~2K instances）→ full scale（~11K）的 degradation pattern：\n\n      At 1K: random baseline 较弱（training set 小，naturally hard negatives 稀少），\n      embedding mining 通过 targeted selection 能显著补充 hard negatives。Delta ≈ +1.2pp。\n\n      At 3K: random baseline 变强，embedding mining marginal advantage 缩小到 +0.5pp。\n\n      At 5K+: random sampling 从足够大的 corpus 中已自动包含 naturally hard negatives \n      （概率论：如果 corpus 中有 p=3% 的 files 与 query cosine similarity > 0.96，\n      随机抽 7 个 negatives 的概率 1-(1-0.03)^7 ≈ 19% 至少包含一个），mining 的 \n      marginal value 趋近于零。\n\n      At 11K (full scale): random baseline 足够强，embed mining 反而可能因为过度集中在 \n      hard region 而导致轻微 overfitting。Delta ≈ -0.17pp。\n\n      这一 scaling curve 是 worst tier 论文的 Fig 5 (main figure for Direction 2)，\n      提供了 mechanistic explanation for why pilot results don't replicate。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: Strategy delta (embed−random) vs training data size\"\n        columns: [Data Size, \"Δ R@1 (pp)\", \"95% CI\", \"Random R@1 baseline\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"1K\", \"+1.2\", \"[+0.1, +2.3]\", \"0.48\"]\n          - [\"3K\", \"+0.5\", \"[-0.4, +1.4]\", \"0.52\"]\n          - [\"5K\", \"+0.2\", \"[-0.7, +1.1]\", \"0.54\"]\n          - [\"11K (full)\", \"-0.17\", \"[-0.92, +0.58]\", \"0.570\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 5 (main): Scaling curve — embed−random delta (pp) vs training data size (log scale)，with 95% CI shading，显示 delta 从 +1.2pp 单调递减至 ~0pp，穿越零线在 ~4K\"\n      - \"Fig 5 inset: Random baseline R@1 vs data size，显示 random 随 data size 单调递增\"\n    analysis: |\n      Scaling analysis 提供了 worst tier 论文的核心 explanatory framework：\n\n      \"Hard negative mining is a data-efficiency technique, not a quality-improvement \n      technique. Its benefit is inversely proportional to training data size because \n      larger corpora naturally contain hard negatives through random sampling.\"\n\n      这一 framing 将 null result 从 \"our method doesn't work\" 转化为 \"we discovered \n      a scaling law for mining effectiveness\"，具有独立的科学价值。\n\n      与 representation geometry analysis 结合：pretrained decoder-only encoders 的\n      near-isotropic representation space 使 random sampling 更有效地覆盖 hard region，\n      进一步减少 targeted mining 的 marginal value。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_009: Fusion Head Ablation\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Fusion head 消融（embedding-only / structural / combined）\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_009\"\n    description: \"测试 structural features 作为 fusion head 输入是否有独立贡献\"\n    expected_results:\n      embedding_only_R1: 0.569\n      structural_only_R1: 0.340\n      combined_R1: 0.571\n      structural_contribution_pp: +0.2\n      structural_contribution_significant: false\n    result_rationale: |\n      Worst tier 下 structural features 的独立贡献微不足道：\n\n      embedding-only 已经非常强（R@1≈0.569，接近 random baseline）。Pretrained decoder-only \n      encoder 的 embedding 质量已经捕获了大部分 file-level similarity signal。\n\n      structural-only（仅用 dataflow features）R@1≈0.340：structural graph features \n      单独提供一些 signal（比 random guessing 强），但远不如 learned embeddings。\n\n      combined（fusion head）R@1≈0.571：几乎无提升（+0.2pp），因为 embedding 已经是 \n      dominant feature，structural features 被 attention weights 自动降权。\n\n      这一结果支持 worst tier narrative：\"pretrained representation quality makes \n      auxiliary features marginal\"。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Confirms that pretrained embeddings dominate. Structural features as fusion input provide no meaningful lift.\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_010: Dataflow-distance Weighted Negatives\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Dataflow-distance weighted negatives vs binary connected/disconnected\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: \"连续权重 vs 二值分类对 dataflow mining 质量的影响\"\n    expected_results:\n      binary_R1: 0.560\n      weighted_R1: 0.558\n      delta_pp: -0.2\n      ci_includes_zero: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      Weighted vs binary 区别在于 negative selection 的粒度：binary 只区分 connected/disconnected，\n      weighted 按 dataflow distance（hop count）给 negatives 赋予连续权重。\n\n      Worst tier 下两者无差异：dataflow strategy 本身 ≈ random，refinement within a null \n      strategy 不会产生 positive effect。Whether you weight by distance or use binary \n      cutoff，最终 selected negatives 在 embedding space 中与 random 不可区分。\n\n      The fundamental issue is not selection granularity but signal relevance：at full scale，\n      structural distance doesn't predict embedding difficulty in a way that improves training。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Minor ablation confirming that refinements to the dataflow strategy don't rescue the null result.\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_011: Failure Analysis\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Failure analysis：50 SweRank/BM25 failures\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: \"分析 50 个 retrieval failure cases，分类 dataflow 是否能帮助\"\n    expected_results:\n      total_failures_analyzed: 50\n      dataflow_could_help: 8\n      dataflow_irrelevant: 32\n      dataflow_would_hurt: 10\n      net_dataflow_potential: \"negative\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Worst tier 下 failure analysis 强化 null result：\n\n      50 个 BM25 failure cases 中：\n      - 8 个（16%）dataflow 能潜在帮助：gold file 在 connected set 中，BM25 排名低\n      - 32 个（64%）dataflow 无关：gold file 要么不在 connected set 中（因为 structural \n        data rate 仅 34%），要么 BM25 已正确排高\n      - 10 个（20%）dataflow 反而有害：structural filtering 排除了 lexically similar \n        但 structurally disconnected 的 gold files\n\n      Net dataflow potential 为负：能帮助的 cases（16%）少于会伤害的 cases（20%）。\n      这与 macro-level null result 一致：dataflow mining 的 structural signal 在 \n      case-by-case 分析中也显示不出 systematic advantage。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Qualitative evidence supporting the quantitative null. Dataflow's structural filtering is as likely to exclude relevant files as to identify hard negatives.\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_012: Qualitative Examples\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"定性 examples：5-10 cases where structural negatives changed retrieval\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: \"展示 structural negatives 改变 retrieval outcome 的具体 cases\"\n    expected_results:\n      positive_examples_found: 3\n      negative_examples_found: 4\n      neutral_examples: 3\n      net_impression: \"mixed — no consistent pattern\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Worst tier 下 qualitative examples 呈现 mixed picture：\n\n      能找到 3 个 positive examples（dataflow-trained model 正确 retrieve 了 structurally \n      connected file），但同时有 4 个 negative examples（dataflow training 导致 model \n      过度偏向 structurally connected files，遗漏 lexically similar gold files）。\n\n      这些 examples 在 worst tier 论文中的定位从 \"showcase of structural benefit\" 变为 \n      \"illustrative cases showing mixed signal\"，支持 \"structural mining is not reliably \n      beneficial\" 的 narrative。\n\n      3 个 neutral examples 中策略选择对 retrieval outcome 无影响（all strategies retrieve \n      same files），进一步支持 null result。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S2: Side-by-side retrieval comparison for 2 positive and 2 negative examples，showing both benefits and harms of structural negatives\"\n    analysis: \"Cherry-picked examples can tell any story. The balanced mixed picture supports the null result narrative.\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_013: StarCoder Full-scale Training (remaining runs)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"M2 全量 StarCoder 3-strategy × 3-seed 训练\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: \"StarCoder2-3B LoRA: random/embed/dataflow × seeds 42/43/44。4 runs 已完成（random ×3, embed s42），预测剩余 5 runs。\"\n    expected_results:\n      # === 已完成 runs（actual data）===\n      random_s42_R1: 0.4604\n      random_s43_R1: 0.4912\n      random_s44_R1: 0.4871\n      random_mean: 0.4796\n      random_std_pp: 1.67\n      embedding_distance_s42_R1: 0.4567\n      # === 预测 runs ===\n      embedding_distance_s43_R1: 0.4880\n      embedding_distance_s44_R1: 0.4830\n      dataflow_aware_s42_R1: 0.4530\n      dataflow_aware_s43_R1: 0.4820\n      dataflow_aware_s44_R1: 0.4780\n      # === 汇总统计 ===\n      embed_mean: 0.4759\n      embed_vs_random_mean_delta_pp: -0.37\n      dataflow_mean: 0.4710\n      dataflow_vs_random_mean_delta_pp: -0.86\n      # === 统计检验 ===\n      embed_vs_random_paired_deltas: [-0.37, -0.32, -0.41]\n      embed_vs_random_bootstrap_95ci: [-0.52, -0.22]\n      embed_vs_random_ci_includes_zero: false\n      dataflow_vs_random_paired_deltas: [-0.74, -0.92, -0.91]\n      dataflow_vs_random_bootstrap_95ci: [-1.02, -0.70]\n      dataflow_vs_random_ci_includes_zero: false\n      starcoder_note: \"Per-encoder CIs exclude zero (embed/dataflow consistently ≤ random), but POOLED cross-encoder CI includes zero\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      StarCoder worst tier 预测：embed 和 dataflow consistently ≤ random。\n\n      embed_s43 预测 0.4880（vs random 0.4912, Δ=-0.32pp）：StarCoder 的 \"healthy\" \n      representation space（pos_sim=0.7985, margin=0.194 for random）意味着 embedding-distance \n      mining 选择的 negatives 过度 hard（neg_sim pushed to 0.741, margin compressed to \n      0.067）。这些 \"too hard\" negatives 导致 training signal noise-dominated，轻微 \n      损害 convergence。\n\n      embed_s44 预测 0.4830（vs random 0.4871, Δ=-0.41pp）：consistent with s42 pattern。\n\n      dataflow_s42-s44 预测一致为 negative delta（-0.74 to -0.92pp）：structural filtering \n      + BM25 ranking 选择的 negatives 在 StarCoder 的 representation space 中既 \n      structurally disconnected 又 lexically similar，但 StarCoder 的 healthy margin \n      已经足够区分——这些 negatives 反而是 \"misleading hard\" rather than \"informative hard\"。\n\n      关键差异 vs Qwen：StarCoder 的 per-encoder CI 可能 exclude zero（all 3 seeds \n      negative），suggesting embed HURTS StarCoder。但 pooled cross-encoder analysis \n      （with Qwen's sign-inconsistent deltas）CI 仍然 includes zero。\n\n      Worst tier narrative interpretation：\n      - Qwen: embed ≈ random（sign-inconsistent，CI includes zero）\n      - StarCoder: embed slightly hurts（consistent negative, CI may exclude zero）\n      - UniXcoder: embed ≈ random（all within 0.37pp）\n      - Cross-encoder pooled: CI includes zero → \"no reliable benefit across architectures\"\n\n      StarCoder embed harm + Qwen embed null = \"mining strategy effect is encoder-dependent \n      but NEVER reliably positive\"。This is worse than \"no effect\" — it's \"unpredictable \n      effect that may be harmful.\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 6: StarCoder2-3B R@1 (best_by_R@1, pool=8)\"\n        columns: [Strategy, s42, s43, s44, \"Mean±Std\", \"Δ vs Random\"]\n        rows:\n          - [random, 0.4604, 0.4912, 0.4871, \"0.4796±0.017\", \"—\"]\n          - [embedding_distance, 0.4567, \"0.4880*\", \"0.4830*\", \"0.4759±0.017\", \"-0.37pp\"]\n          - [dataflow_aware, \"0.4530*\", \"0.4820*\", \"0.4780*\", \"0.4710±0.016\", \"-0.86pp\"]\n        note: \"* = predicted. StarCoder per-encoder CIs may exclude zero (consistent negative deltas), but pooled cross-encoder CI includes zero.\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 6: Qwen vs StarCoder paired delta comparison — showing Qwen sign-inconsistent vs StarCoder consistently negative\"\n    analysis: |\n      StarCoder 结果是 worst tier 中最 damaging 的 evidence：pilot pattern（embed +1.6pp）\n      在 full scale 完全反转为 consistently negative。这一 \"pilot → full scale degradation\" \n      pattern 是 Direction 2（negative result study）的核心叙事支撑。\n\n      与 representation geometry 的关系：StarCoder 的 healthy margin（0.194 for random）\n      被 embed mining 压缩至 0.067，loss of margin diversity 可能是 performance degradation \n      的 mechanism。但在 worst tier 下，这个 mechanism 的 explanatory power 有限——\n      它解释了 WHY embed hurts StarCoder，但不能 prescriptively 告诉 practitioners 何时 \n      mining 会 help。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_014: Temperature Ablation (Full)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Temperature 消融（τ ∈ {0.05, 0.1, 0.2}）\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: \"3 个 temperature × 3 strategies × 3 seeds × Qwen，测试 strategy ranking 的 regime-specificity\"\n    expected_results:\n      # === τ=0.05 ===\n      tau005_random_R1_mean: 0.555\n      tau005_embed_R1_mean: 0.552\n      tau005_embed_vs_random_pp: -0.3\n      tau005_strategy_ranking: \"random ≈ embed ≈ dataflow\"\n      # === τ=0.1 (baseline) ===\n      tau010_note: \"τ=0.07 in actual config, τ=0.1 in plan — using actual τ=0.07 data\"\n      tau010_embed_vs_random_pp: -0.17\n      # === τ=0.2 ===\n      tau020_random_R1_mean: 0.548\n      tau020_embed_R1_mean: 0.546\n      tau020_embed_vs_random_pp: -0.2\n      tau020_strategy_ranking: \"random ≈ embed ≈ dataflow\"\n      # === overall ===\n      strategy_ranking_changes_with_tau: false\n      null_result_regime_independent: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      Worst tier 下 temperature 不影响 strategy ranking（永远都是 null）：\n\n      τ=0.05（sharper distribution）：更强的 gradient signal，但对所有 strategies 等量增强。\n      Absolute R@1 微降（training 不太稳定，容易 overfit），但 strategy delta 仍在 noise \n      floor 内。Embed vs random ≈ -0.3pp（CI includes zero）。\n\n      τ=0.2（smoother distribution）：更弱的 gradient signal，所有 strategies 等量减弱。\n      Absolute R@1 微降（gradient 太弱，学习不充分），strategy delta 仍 ≈ 0。\n\n      关键论据：如果 embed mining 的 advantage 是 regime-specific（仅在 τ=0.05 出现），\n      则 pilot 的 positive result 可以归因于 τ 选择。但 worst tier 下 ALL temperatures \n      都是 null，排除了 \"wrong temperature regime\" 作为 null result 的 explanation。\n\n      这一结果强化 null result 的 robustness：\"mining strategy effect is not hidden in \n      a different temperature regime — it genuinely doesn't exist at this scale.\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S1: Embed−random delta (pp) by temperature\"\n        columns: [\"τ\", \"Δ R@1 (pp)\", \"95% CI\", \"Abs Random R@1\"]\n        rows:\n          - [0.05, \"-0.3\", \"[-1.1, +0.5]\", 0.555]\n          - [0.07, \"-0.17\", \"[-0.92, +0.58]\", 0.570]\n          - [0.2, \"-0.2\", \"[-1.0, +0.6]\", 0.548]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S3: Strategy delta vs temperature curve，showing flat (null) pattern across τ values\"\n    analysis: \"Temperature ablation confirms null result is regime-independent. No τ value rescues mining strategy effectiveness.\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_015: Dynamic Mining Baseline\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Dynamic embedding mining baseline\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_015\"\n    description: \"每 epoch 重新 mine embedding negatives vs static（一次 mine from pretrained），隔离 selection criterion vs curriculum shift\"\n    expected_results:\n      static_embed_R1_mean: 0.568\n      dynamic_embed_R1_mean: 0.567\n      dynamic_vs_static_pp: -0.1\n      dynamic_vs_random_pp: -0.27\n      ci_includes_zero: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      Dynamic mining 与 static mining 无差异：\n\n      Static mining 从 pretrained encoder mine negatives（one-shot）。Dynamic mining \n      每个 epoch 用 updated encoder 重新 mine。如果 static mining 的 problem 是 \n      \"stale negatives\"（encoder 学习后 difficulty ranking 变化），dynamic mining 应该 \n      显著改善。\n\n      Worst tier 下 dynamic ≈ static ≈ random，因为：\n      1. Encoder 在 LoRA fine-tuning 后 representation 变化很小（LoRA rank=16，仅更新 \n         0.5% 参数），difficulty ranking 几乎不变\n      2. 即使 difficulty ranking 更新了，mining 的 marginal value 在 full-scale data \n         下已经为零——更 fresh 的 negatives 不会改变这个 fundamental limitation\n      3. Dynamic mining 的 computational overhead（每 epoch 重新 encode 全 corpus + \n         nearest neighbor search）相当于 ~10% training time，ROI 为零\n\n      这一结果排除了 \"static vs dynamic\" confound 作为 null result 的 explanation。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Dynamic mining doesn't rescue the null. The problem isn't stale negatives — it's that mining signal is fundamentally marginal at full scale.\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_016: Bootstrap CI for SWE-bench\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"SWE-bench Bootstrap CI\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_016\"\n    description: \"为 SWE-bench Lite resolve rate 添加 95% bootstrap CI\"\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"DROPPED — SWE-bench abandoned\"\n      if_computed:\n        R1: 0.04\n        bootstrap_95ci: [0.01, 0.08]\n        note: \"CI confirms OOD failure is real, not sample noise\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      SWE-bench 已被放弃（R@1=0.04 vs BM25=0.2733）。即使计算 bootstrap CI，也只是 \n      确认 OOD failure 是 real（CI [0.01, 0.08] 远低于 BM25 baseline）。\n\n      在 worst tier 论文中不提 SWE-bench。这意味着论文缺少 downstream task evaluation，\n      是一个 acknowledged limitation。RepoBench-R（plan_004）是唯一的 external validation。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"N/A. SWE-bench dropped from paper. External validation relies entirely on RepoBench-R.\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_018: BM25 Negative Baseline (Training Phase)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"BM25 negative baseline 训练\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_018\"\n    description: \"Phase 1 (mining) 已完成，Phase 2: 训练 BM25 negatives × 3 seeds Qwen + 1 seed StarCoder\"\n    expected_results:\n      # === Phase 1 actual data ===\n      phase1_bm25_mining_done: true\n      bm25_vs_embedding_overlap_k50: 0.871\n      bm25_vs_random_overlap_k50: 0.762\n      # === Phase 2 Qwen training predictions ===\n      qwen_bm25_s42_R1: 0.555\n      qwen_bm25_s43_R1: 0.558\n      qwen_bm25_s44_R1: 0.597\n      qwen_bm25_mean: 0.570\n      qwen_bm25_vs_random_mean_pp: +0.03\n      qwen_bm25_vs_random_ci: [-0.55, +0.59]\n      qwen_bm25_ci_includes_zero: true\n      # === Phase 2 StarCoder training predictions ===\n      starcoder_bm25_s42_R1: 0.459\n      starcoder_bm25_vs_random_s42_pp: -0.14\n      # === Cross-strategy comparison ===\n      bm25_vs_embed_qwen_mean_pp: +0.20\n      bm25_vs_embed_starcoder_s42_pp: +0.24\n      bm25_strategy_ranking: \"bm25 ≈ random > embed ≈ dataflow (but all within noise)\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      BM25 ≈ random 是 worst tier 的 critical prediction，devastating for CoCoHaNeRe narrative。\n\n      Phase 1 overlap analysis 已经 foreshadowed this：BM25 和 embedding negatives 87.1% \n      重叠（k=50 level）。在 large repos（200+ files）中 overlap 下降至 29.7%（Jaccard \n      top-7），但这些 repos 中 BM25 和 embedding 选择的 negatives 在 cosine similarity \n      distribution 上仍然高度相似。\n\n      Qwen BM25 训练预测：3 seeds mean Δ = +0.03pp（essentially zero）。BM25 negatives \n      既不 harm（反驳 MVP artifact where BM25-proxy caused -27pp，那是 labeling bug）也不 \n      help（BM25 similarity ≠ embedding difficulty in a way that improves training）。\n\n      StarCoder BM25 预测：Δ = -0.14pp（also ≈ zero）。\n\n      CoCoHaNeRe narrative 失效分析：\n      1. CoCoHaNeRe 声称 gradient-based mining >> non-differentiable embedding mining\n      2. 我们的原始叙事：simple embedding mining provides reliable improvement（反驳 CoCoHaNeRe）\n      3. Worst tier 下：BM25 ≈ embed ≈ random → 所有 non-gradient methods 都 ≈ random\n      4. 但我们也不能说 gradient-based methods 更好（未测试）\n      5. 结论：在我们的 setting 下，mining strategy choice doesn't matter at all，无法对 \n         CoCoHaNeRe 的 gradient-based claim 做有意义的评论\n\n      4-strategy comparison 中的微妙 pattern：bm25 ≈ random > embed ≈ dataflow（numerically, \n      not significantly）。这可能暗示 embed 和 dataflow 的 targeted hard negatives 轻微 \n      有害，而 BM25 的 \"untargeted lexical similarity\" 恰好与 random 等效。但 effect sizes \n      全部在 noise floor 内。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 7: 4-Strategy comparison (Qwen, mean across 3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [Strategy, \"R@1 Mean±Std\", \"Δ vs Random (pp)\", \"95% CI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [random, \"0.570±0.027\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [embedding_distance, \"0.568±0.023\", \"-0.17\", \"[-0.92, +0.58]\"]\n          - [dataflow_aware, \"0.560±0.014\", \"-0.99\", \"[-2.36, +0.58]\"]\n          - [bm25, \"0.570±0.023\", \"+0.03\", \"[-0.55, +0.59]\"]\n        note: \"All 95% CIs include zero. Mining strategy ≈ noise.\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 7: 4-strategy comparison bar chart with error bars，showing all strategies clustered around random baseline\"\n      - \"Fig 8: BM25-embedding negative overlap heatmap by repo size tier，showing 87% overlap at corpus level\"\n    analysis: |\n      BM25 null result 完成了 worst tier 的最后一块拼图：\n\n      4 种 mining strategies（random, embedding, dataflow, bm25）全部 ≈ random。\n      This is not \"embedding is the best non-gradient method\" (original narrative) \n      nor \"BM25 is harmful\" (CoCoHaNeRe narrative) — it's \"nothing matters at this scale.\"\n\n      Paper framing 必须完全 reframe：从 \"which strategy is best\" 转变为 \n      \"why does strategy choice not matter\" + \"what does matter (checkpoint criterion).\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_019: Pool Size Sensitivity\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Pool size sensitivity（pool={50, 100, 200, 500}）\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_019\"\n    description: \"测试 strategy ranking 在 realistic pool sizes 下的稳定性\"\n    expected_results:\n      # === Qwen results by pool size ===\n      qwen_pool_8:\n        random_R1: 0.570\n        embed_R1: 0.568\n        delta_pp: -0.17\n        strategy_ranking: \"random ≈ embed\"\n      qwen_pool_50:\n        random_R1: 0.420\n        embed_R1: 0.415\n        delta_pp: -0.5\n        strategy_ranking: \"random > embed (but CI includes zero)\"\n      qwen_pool_100:\n        random_R1: 0.310\n        embed_R1: 0.308\n        delta_pp: -0.2\n        strategy_ranking: \"indistinguishable\"\n      qwen_pool_200:\n        random_R1: 0.210\n        embed_R1: 0.208\n        delta_pp: -0.2\n        strategy_ranking: \"indistinguishable\"\n      qwen_pool_500:\n        random_R1: 0.115\n        embed_R1: 0.113\n        delta_pp: -0.2\n        strategy_ranking: \"indistinguishable\"\n      # === Pool size effect vs strategy effect ===\n      pool_8_to_500_random_drop_pp: 45.5\n      strategy_delta_at_pool_500_pp: 0.2\n      pool_to_strategy_ratio: \"227x\"\n      ranking_reversal_observed: true\n      ranking_reversal_pool: 50\n      ranking_reversal_note: \"At pool=50, embed vs random delta is -0.5pp (embed worse), while at pool=8 it's -0.17pp. Direction consistent but magnitude varies with pool size.\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Pool size sensitivity 是 worst tier 论文的 decisive evidence。\n\n      Predictions 基于两个 mechanisms：\n      1. Pool size 增大时，absolute R@1 单调下降（更多 distractors → harder retrieval）。\n         Pool=8 → pool=500 的 R@1 drop ≈ 45pp，远超任何 strategy effect。\n      2. Strategy differences 被 proportionally compressed：如果 strategy effect 是 \n         multiplicative（improves relative ranking），larger pool 应该 preserve delta。\n         但如果 effect 是 additive noise（which worst tier assumes），larger pool 中 \n         delta 保持 absolute size 而 relative importance shrinks。\n\n      Worst tier 预测：strategy ranking 在 pool>50 时实质性消失。Pool=50 时 embed \n      已经比 random 差 0.5pp（consistent with pilot data showing -3.7pp at pool=50, \n      but full-scale model is better trained）。Pool=100+ 时 delta 压缩到 <0.3pp。\n\n      ranking_reversal 在 pool=50 观察到：embed vs random 从 pool=8 的 -0.17pp 扩大到 \n      pool=50 的 -0.5pp（negative direction amplified）。这意味着 embed mining 在 \n      larger pools 中的 slight harm 被放大——consistent with \"too hard negatives cause \n      slight overfitting that hurts at realistic retrieval difficulty。\"\n\n      论文 contribution：pool size sensitivity analysis 证明现有 mining strategy 文献的 \n      reported gains（在 pool=5-20 的 tiny val sets 上评估）不 generalize to realistic \n      retrieval scenarios（pool=100-500+）。这是 evaluation methodology warning 的 \n      additional evidence。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 8: Qwen R@1 by pool size (mean across 3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [Pool Size, Random, Embed, Dataflow, \"Embed−Random (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [8, 0.570, 0.568, 0.560, \"-0.17\"]\n          - [50, 0.420, 0.415, 0.408, \"-0.5\"]\n          - [100, 0.310, 0.308, 0.303, \"-0.2\"]\n          - [200, 0.210, 0.208, 0.205, \"-0.2\"]\n          - [500, 0.115, 0.113, 0.111, \"-0.2\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 9 (main): R@1 vs pool size curve for each strategy，showing parallel decline with no strategy separation\"\n      - \"Fig 9 inset: Strategy delta vs pool size，showing delta stays near zero across all pool sizes\"\n    analysis: |\n      Pool size sensitivity 证明 worst tier 的 scale-dependent argument：\n\n      \"Mining strategy evaluations conducted on small validation pools (pool < 20) \n      measure pool-size-dependent retrieval ease, not strategy-dependent improvement. \n      At realistic pool sizes (100+), strategy differences vanish entirely.\"\n\n      Combined with plan_008 (data scaling) and plan_005 (stratification), this forms \n      a comprehensive negative result: mining strategy effect disappears along EVERY \n      scaling dimension (data size, pool size, and subpopulation).\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_020: UniXcoder Multi-seed Validation\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"UniXcoder 多种子验证（s42/s43/s44）\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_020\"\n    description: \"UniXcoder-base (125M, encoder-only) 上 3-strategy × 3-seed 验证 cross-architecture generalization\"\n    expected_results:\n      # === s42 actual ===\n      s42_random_R1: 0.5534\n      s42_embed_R1: 0.5497\n      s42_dataflow_R1: 0.5510\n      s42_strategy_range_pp: 0.37\n      # === s43 predictions ===\n      s43_random_R1: 0.577\n      s43_embed_R1: 0.573\n      s43_dataflow_R1: 0.575\n      s43_strategy_range_pp: 0.4\n      # === s44 predictions ===\n      s44_random_R1: 0.560\n      s44_embed_R1: 0.556\n      s44_dataflow_R1: 0.558\n      s44_strategy_range_pp: 0.4\n      # === cross-seed summary ===\n      random_mean: 0.5635\n      random_std_pp: 1.2\n      embed_mean: 0.5596\n      embed_vs_random_mean_pp: -0.39\n      embed_vs_random_ci: [-0.85, +0.07]\n      embed_vs_random_ci_includes_zero: true\n      dataflow_mean: 0.5613\n      dataflow_vs_random_mean_pp: -0.22\n      cross_seed_std_dominates: true\n      # === cross-architecture synthesis ===\n      three_encoder_null: true\n      architecture_types_tested: [\"encoder-only (UniXcoder 125M)\", \"decoder-only (Qwen 3B)\", \"decoder-only (StarCoder 3B)\"]\n    result_rationale: |\n      UniXcoder 在 worst tier 中提供 3rd architecture confirmation of null result。\n\n      UniXcoder-base（125M, encoder-only, RoBERTa-based）与 Qwen/StarCoder（3B, \n      decoder-only）架构完全不同。如果 mining strategy effect 在 125M encoder-only \n      model 上也是 null，则结论的 generality 大幅增强。\n\n      s42 actual data 已显示 0.37pp 全 range（远小于 noise floor）。Worst tier 预测 \n      s43/s44 同样 null（0.4pp range per seed），cross-seed std（1.2pp）远大于 \n      within-seed strategy delta（<0.4pp）。\n\n      Three-encoder null result 的论证力度：\n      1. UniXcoder 125M (encoder-only): null → 不是模型太小的问题\n      2. Qwen 3B (decoder-only, FIM pretrained): null → 不是 Qwen-specific\n      3. StarCoder 3B (decoder-only, code-specific): embed hurts → 更差\n      \n      Cross-architecture generalization：\"no evidence mining strategy matters at this scale, \n      regardless of architecture choice (encoder-only vs decoder-only), model size (125M \n      vs 3B), and pretraining strategy (masked LM vs FIM vs code-specific).\"\n\n      UniXcoder 的额外价值：它的 pos_sim 接近 Qwen（高 similarity, near-saturated），\n      但架构完全不同。这排除了 \"saturation is decoder-only artifact\" 的 objection。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 9: UniXcoder-base R@1 (best_by_R@1, pool=8)\"\n        columns: [Strategy, s42, s43, s44, \"Mean±Std\", \"Δ vs Random\"]\n        rows:\n          - [random, 0.5534, \"0.577*\", \"0.560*\", \"0.564±0.012\", \"—\"]\n          - [embedding_distance, 0.5497, \"0.573*\", \"0.556*\", \"0.560±0.012\", \"-0.39pp\"]\n          - [dataflow_aware, 0.5510, \"0.575*\", \"0.558*\", \"0.561±0.012\", \"-0.22pp\"]\n        note: \"* = predicted. Strategy range <0.4pp per seed.\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 10: Three-encoder comparison panel — R@1 by strategy for Qwen/StarCoder/UniXcoder with 95% CIs，showing universal null\"\n    analysis: |\n      UniXcoder multi-seed 完成了 cross-architecture validation。三种不同架构 × 三种不同 \n      model sizes × 三种不同 pretraining strategies 全部显示 null result。\n\n      This level of consistency across architectures is actually a STRONG finding — \n      it's just a negative one. The paper can claim: \"We provide the most comprehensive \n      evidence to date that hard negative mining strategies do not reliably improve \n      contrastive code retrieval at training scales of 10K+ instances.\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_021: Temperature Ablation (Reduced)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Temperature 消融（reduced scope: τ={0.05, 0.2} × random+embed × Qwen × s42）\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_021\"\n    description: \"Reduced scope of plan_014: 4 runs total to verify regime-specificity\"\n    expected_results:\n      tau005_random_s42_R1: 0.548\n      tau005_embed_s42_R1: 0.545\n      tau005_delta_pp: -0.3\n      tau020_random_s42_R1: 0.540\n      tau020_embed_s42_R1: 0.538\n      tau020_delta_pp: -0.2\n      regime_specificity_confirmed: false\n      null_at_all_temperatures: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      Reduced scope 足以 falsify \"τ=0.07 是 null 的原因\" 假说。\n\n      两个极端温度（0.05 sharp, 0.2 smooth）都显示 embed ≈ random（delta -0.2 to -0.3pp）。\n      Strategy ranking 不随 τ 变化。Absolute R@1 在极端 τ 时微降（training less optimal），\n      但 relative strategy performance 保持 null。\n\n      4 runs（15h GPU）足以 rule out regime-specificity concern。Full plan_014（70h）\n      在 worst tier 下 not justified — 已知 null result 是 regime-independent。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Minimal evidence needed to rule out temperature regime as explanation for null result.\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Additional worst-tier required experiments (not in current plan)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"额外 seeds 确认 null（5-10 seeds）\"\n    plan_id: \"worst_extra_a\"\n    description: \"在 Qwen 上扩展至 5-10 seeds（embed + random），power analysis 确认需要多少 seeds 才能 detect 0.3pp effect\"\n    expected_results:\n      seeds_5_embed_vs_random_mean_pp: -0.10\n      seeds_5_ci: [-0.45, +0.25]\n      seeds_5_ci_includes_zero: true\n      seeds_10_embed_vs_random_mean_pp: -0.08\n      seeds_10_ci: [-0.30, +0.14]\n      seeds_10_ci_includes_zero: true\n      power_analysis:\n        detectable_effect_at_80_power_3seeds_pp: 2.5\n        detectable_effect_at_80_power_5seeds_pp: 1.5\n        detectable_effect_at_80_power_10seeds_pp: 0.8\n        seeds_needed_for_0.3pp_effect: \">50\"\n        conclusion: \"Even 10 seeds cannot reliably detect 0.3pp effects given cross-seed std of 2.7pp\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Power analysis 揭示 fundamental limitation：with cross-seed std ≈ 2.7pp，detecting \n      a 0.3pp effect at 80% power requires >50 seeds（paired t-test, α=0.05）。\n\n      扩展至 5-10 seeds 不会改变 conclusion（CI 仍 includes zero），但会 sharpen the \n      null：从 \"can't detect\" 到 \"can confidently bound effect < 0.8pp\"。\n\n      这也成为 methodological contribution：prior work reporting 1-2pp gains from mining \n      strategies with 1-3 seeds is statistically inadequate. Our power analysis shows \n      minimum 10 seeds needed to detect effects in the 1pp range for this task。\n\n      Worst tier 论文 should include this power analysis as Table in methodology section。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 10: Power analysis for strategy effect detection\"\n        columns: [Seeds, \"Detectable Effect (pp, 80% power)\", \"Estimated 95% CI width (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [3, 2.5, 2.9]\n          - [5, 1.5, 2.2]\n          - [10, 0.8, 1.5]\n          - [50, 0.3, 0.7]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: |\n      Power analysis 是 worst tier 论文（Direction 1: Methodology Warning）的 key table。\n      它直接挑战 prior work 的 statistical adequacy，属于 community-level methodological \n      contribution，不依赖于我们自己的 positive findings。\n\n  - name: \"Scaling analysis（data size vs strategy effect）\"\n    plan_id: \"worst_extra_b\"\n    description: \"Same as plan_008 but framed as worst tier's required additional experiment\"\n    expected_results:\n      note: \"See plan_008 predictions above — same experiment\"\n    result_rationale: \"Already covered under plan_008. Required for Direction 2 (negative result study) core figure.\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Cross-reference with plan_008.\"\n\n  - name: \"Published mining paper reproduction attempt\"\n    plan_id: \"worst_extra_c\"\n    description: \"Attempt to reproduce 1-2 published hard negative mining papers' claims in our setting\"\n    expected_results:\n      paper_1_name: \"CoCoHaNeRe (TOSEM 2025)\"\n      paper_1_claimed_gain_pp: 3.5\n      paper_1_reproduced_gain_pp: 0.2\n      paper_1_reproduced_ci: [-0.8, +1.2]\n      paper_1_reproduced_significant: false\n      paper_2_name: \"ANCE (ICLR 2021)\"\n      paper_2_claimed_gain_pp: 2.8\n      paper_2_reproduced_gain_pp: 0.4\n      paper_2_reproduced_ci: [-0.5, +1.3]\n      paper_2_reproduced_significant: false\n      reproduction_conclusion: \"Neither paper's claimed gains replicate in our controlled setting with multi-seed CIs\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Reproduction attempt 在 worst tier 下会失败：prior work 的 reported gains 在我们的 \n      controlled setting（multi-seed, fixed pool, proper CI）下不 replicate。\n\n      可能原因：\n      1. Prior work 使用 single seed + cherry-picked checkpoint（our D062 finding）\n      2. Prior work 评估在 small pools（our plan_019 finding）\n      3. Prior work 数据规模更小（our plan_008 finding）\n      4. Prior work 使用不同 base models（但 UniXcoder null 表明 architecture isn't the issue）\n\n      Reproduction failure 为 worst tier 论文提供 strongest possible evidence：不仅我们的 \n      mining strategies 无效，prior work 声称有效的 strategies 在 properly controlled \n      setting 下也无效。\n\n      这一 experiment 把 worst tier 论文从 \"our specific methods don't work\" 提升为 \n      \"the field's claims about mining effectiveness may be statistical artifacts\"——\n      这是 EMNLP Main 级别的 contribution。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: |\n      Reproduction attempt 是 worst tier 论文最有野心的 contribution。如果成功证明 \n      prior work 不 replicate，论文变成对整个 hard negative mining 文献的 meta-methodological \n      critique，与 \"checkpoint criterion > mining strategy\" 主题完美呼应。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Checkpoint Criterion Effect (D062) — Core Worst Tier Finding\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Checkpoint selection criterion effect 综合分析\"\n    plan_id: \"D062_synthesis\"\n    description: \"量化 checkpoint 选择标准（best_by_R@1 vs best_by_val_loss）在完整 4-strategy × 3-seed × 3-encoder 矩阵中造成的报告差异\"\n    expected_results:\n      # === Per-run criterion divergence ===\n      per_run_R1_gap_mean_pp: 1.3\n      per_run_R1_gap_max_pp: 2.0\n      per_run_R1_gap_min_pp: 0.0\n      runs_where_criteria_pick_different_step: \"12/18 (67%)\"\n      # === Strategy ranking affected by criterion ===\n      ranking_flips_by_criterion: 3\n      ranking_flip_example: \"Qwen s44: by R@1 → random best; by val_loss → random best (same); but Qwen s43: by R@1 → embed best; by val_loss → random best (flip)\"\n      # === Combined methodological variance ===\n      total_analyst_flexibility_pp: 15.2\n      composed_of:\n        checkpoint_criterion_contribution_pp: 3.5\n        seed_selection_contribution_pp: 5.0\n        pool_size_contribution_pp: 6.7\n      strategy_effect_in_context_pp: 0.5\n      methodology_to_strategy_ratio: \"30x\"\n      # === Robust checkpoint effect (the surviving finding) ===\n      checkpoint_criterion_effect_pp: 14.8\n      checkpoint_criterion_robust_across_seeds: true\n      checkpoint_criterion_robust_across_encoders: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      D062 checkpoint criterion effect 是 worst tier 唯一幸存的核心发现。\n\n      effect 的构成（~15pp total analyst flexibility）：\n      1. Checkpoint 选择标准（3.5pp）：同一个 run 中，best_by_R@1 checkpoint 的 R@1 比 \n         best_by_val_loss checkpoint 的 R@1 高 0-2pp（mean 1.3pp）。67% 的 runs 中两个 \n         criteria 选择不同的 checkpoint。在 3 strategies × 3 seeds matrix 中，这会导致 \n         strategy ranking flip（3 次 observed）。\n      2. Seed 选择（5.0pp）：Qwen random cross-seed range = 0.5527-0.6009 = 4.82pp。\n         Cherry-picking best vs worst seed 造成 ~5pp 报告差异。\n      3. Pool size（6.7pp）：从 val pool=8 到 realistic pool=50，R@1 下降 ~15pp；\n         但 relative strategy ranking 可能 flip（pilot 中 embed 在 pool=8 好但 pool=50 差）。\n         Pool size 选择在论文中通常不报告，是 hidden methodology choice。\n\n      Strategy effect（0.5pp）在这 15pp analyst flexibility space 中仅占 3.3%。\n\n      这一分析的论证力度：不是说研究者会恶意 cherry-pick，而是说在 standard practice 中\n      （选 best checkpoint，选 best seed for reporting，使用 convenient pool size for eval），\n      methodological choices 的 variance 远远大于 effect being studied。This is a genuine \n      methodological contribution that doesn't depend on our specific mining strategies。\n\n      Robustness：checkpoint criterion effect 在 all 3 encoders × all 3 seeds 上一致 \n      存在（val_loss-best 和 R@1-best 经常 diverge），不是 encoder-specific 或 seed-specific。\n      这使它成为 generalizable finding，适合 EMNLP Main 发表。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 11: Checkpoint criterion effect — R@1 gap between best_by_R@1 and best_by_val_loss checkpoint\"\n        columns: [Encoder, Strategy, Seed, \"R@1 (best_by_R@1)\", \"R@1 (best_by_val_loss)\", \"Gap (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [Qwen, random, s42, 0.5527, 0.5527, 0.0]\n          - [Qwen, random, s43, 0.5554, 0.5357, +1.97]\n          - [Qwen, random, s44, 0.6009, 0.6009, 0.0]\n          - [Qwen, embed, s43, 0.5606, 0.5446, +1.60]\n          - [Qwen, embed, s44, 0.5942, 0.5813, +1.29]\n          - [\"StarCoder*\", random, s42, 0.4604, 0.4537, +0.67]\n          - [\"StarCoder*\", random, s43, 0.4912, 0.4912, 0.0]\n          - [\"StarCoder*\", random, s44, 0.4871, 0.4848, +0.23]\n        note: \"Mean gap: 0.72pp per run. 5/8 runs show criterion divergence. * = actual data for completed runs.\"\n      - name: \"Table 12: Analyst flexibility decomposition\"\n        columns: [Source, \"Variance (pp)\", \"% of total\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Checkpoint criterion (R@1 vs val_loss)\", 3.5, \"23%\"]\n          - [\"Seed selection (best vs worst)\", 5.0, \"33%\"]\n          - [\"Pool size (val pool=8 vs realistic pool=50+)\", 6.7, \"44%\"]\n          - [\"TOTAL methodology variance\", 15.2, \"100%\"]\n          - [\"Mining strategy effect\", 0.5, \"3.3% of methodology variance\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 11 (main): Paired plot showing R@1 at best_by_R@1 vs best_by_val_loss checkpoint for each run，connected by lines showing criterion divergence\"\n      - \"Fig 12: Variance decomposition pie chart — methodology (96.7%) vs strategy (3.3%)\"\n    analysis: |\n      D062 synthesis 提供了 worst tier 论文的 central message：\n\n      \"In contrastive code retrieval, methodological choices in checkpoint selection, \n      seed reporting, and evaluation pool size create 30x more variance in reported \n      results than the mining strategy choice being studied. Before the field can make \n      reliable claims about mining strategy effectiveness, evaluation methodology \n      must be standardized.\"\n\n      这是一个 strong EMNLP Main contribution because：\n      1. It's quantitative (15.2pp vs 0.5pp)\n      2. It generalizes beyond code (applies to any contrastive learning with checkpoint selection)\n      3. It's actionable (researchers can adopt our proposed evaluation protocol)\n      4. It explains prior contradictions in mining literature (different papers use different \n         checkpoint criteria, seeds, pool sizes → conflicting conclusions)\n\n      建议的 evaluation protocol（论文 Section 5 contribution）：\n      - 最少 5 seeds（power analysis shows 3 is inadequate）\n      - Report both best_by_R@1 and best_by_val_loss checkpoints\n      - Evaluate at multiple pool sizes（at least pool=50 and pool=200）\n      - Use paired within-seed comparisons with cluster bootstrap CIs\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"e9214298-f5a6-4448-a682-aa14a7b561f2","total_cost_usd":1.6591984000000002,"usage":{"input_tokens":4792,"cache_creation_input_tokens":38639,"cache_read_input_tokens":85638,"output_tokens":47635,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":38639,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4789,"output_tokens":47124,"cache_read_input_tokens":38135,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12345,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12345},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":18874,"outputTokens":6326,"cacheReadInputTokens":456029,"cacheCreationInputTokens":51155,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.16005065,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":4792,"outputTokens":47635,"cacheReadInputTokens":85638,"cacheCreationInputTokens":38639,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.4991477500000001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"b6016fef-394e-4697-80c6-c02c9095b141"}
